helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	ga	You can open and close the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> Bar in \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Java Platform Support				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153089				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0650.xhp\" name=\"Java Platform Support\"\>Java Platform Support\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	ga	$[officename] supports the Java platform for running applications and components based on the JavaBeans architecture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ga	For $[officename] to support the Java platform, you must install the Java 2 Runtime Environment software. When you installed $[officename], you automatically received the option to install these files if they were not yet installed. You can also install these files now if required.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	ga	The Java platform support needs to be activated under $[officename] to run Java applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	ga	Activate Java platform support by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/java.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Java\"\>$[officename] - Java\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id9116183				0	ga	Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME- Java, and click the Class Path button. After you add the path information, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	ga	Your modifications at the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Java\</emph\> tab page will be used even if the Java Virtual Machine (JVM, a virtual machine for the Java platform) already has been started. After modifications to the ClassPath you must restart $[officename]. The same is true for modifications under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Internet - Proxy\</emph\>. Only the two boxes "Http Proxy" and "Ftp Proxy" and their ports don't require a restart, they will be evaluated when you click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
