helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	ga	This section contains descriptions of frequently used shortcut keys in $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Edit Points Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>lines; editing points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves; editing points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Edit Points bar\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149987				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0227.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points Bar\"\>Edit Points Bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150402				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BEZIER_TOOLBOX\"\>The \<emph\>Edit Points \</emph\>Bar appears when you select a polygon object and click \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	ga	The functions provided allow you to edit the points of a curve or an object converted to a curve. The following icons are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153105				0	ga	Edit Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3159151				0	ga	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points\"\>\<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>\</link\> icon allows you to activate or deactivate the edit mode for Bézier objects. In the edit mode, individual points of the drawing object can be selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3153951\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153951\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	ga	Edit Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	ga	Move Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierMove\"\>Activates a mode in which you can move points.\</ahelp\> The mouse pointer displays a small empty square when resting on a point. Drag that point to another location. The curve on both sides of the point follows the movement; the section of the curve between the next points changes shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	ga	Point at the curve between two points or within a closed curve and drag the mouse to shift the entire curve without distorting the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3149377\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziermove.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149377\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	ga	Move Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150115				0	ga	Insert Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3160478				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierInsert\"\>Activates the insert mode. This mode allows you to insert points.\</ahelp\> You can also move points, just as in the move mode. If, however, you click at the curve between two points and move the mouse a little while holding down the mouse button you insert a new point. The point is a smooth point, and the lines to the control points are parallel and remain so when moved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3157846				0	ga	If you wish to create a corner point you must first insert either a smooth or a symmetrical point which is then converted to a corner point by using \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3146969\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146969\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	ga	Insert Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149020				0	ga	Delete Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148917				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierDelete\"\>Use the \<emph\>Delete Points\</emph\> icon to delete one or several selected points. If you wish to select several points click the appropriate points while holding down the Shift key.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153766				0	ga	First select the points to be deleted, and then click this icon, or press Del.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147321				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3146920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierdelete.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155961				0	ga	Delete Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	ga	Split Curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierCutLine\"\>The\<emph\> Split Curve \</emph\>icon splits a curve. Select the point or points where you want to split the curve, then click the icon\</ahelp\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153788				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziercutline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152581				0	ga	Split Curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	ga	Convert To Curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148420				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierConvert\"\>Converts a curve into a straight line or converts a straight line into a curve.\</ahelp\> If you select a single point, the curve before the point will be converted. If two points are selected, the curve between both points will be converted. If you select more than two points, each time you click this icon, a different portion of the curve will be converted. If necessary, round points are converted into corner points and corner points are converted into round points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	ga	If a certain section of the curve is straight, the end points of the line have a maximum of one control point each. They cannot be modified to round points unless the straight line is converted back to a curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158212				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3149036\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierconvert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149036\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158445				0	ga	Convert To Curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153199				0	ga	Corner Point				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148460				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEdge\"\>Converts the selected point or points into corner points.\</ahelp\> Corner points have two movable control points, which are independent from each other. A curved line, therefore, does not go straight through a corner point, but forms a corner.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154576				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3154201\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezieredge.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154201\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429				0	ga	Corner Point				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166436				0	ga	Smooth Transition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155510				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSmooth\"\>Converts a corner point or symmetrical point into a smooth point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel, and can only be moved simultaneously. The control points may differentiate in length, allowing you to vary the degree of curvature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3151183\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersmooth.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151183\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	ga	Smooth Transition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159622				0	ga	Symmetric Transition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155812				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSymmetric\"\>This icon converts a corner point or a smooth point into a symmetrical point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel and have the same length. They can only be moved simultaneously and the degree of curvature is the same in both directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3159218\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersymmetric.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159218\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3146866				0	ga	Symmetric Transition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146786				0	ga	Close Bézier				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierClose\"\>Closes a line or a curve.\</ahelp\> A line is closed by connecting the last point with the first point, indicated by an enlarged square.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3148607\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierclose.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148607\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147070				0	ga	Close Bézier				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156351				0	ga	Eliminate Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149441				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEliminatePoints\"\>Marks the current point or the selected points for deletion.\</ahelp\> This happens in the event that the point is located on a straight line. If you convert a curve or a polygon with the \<emph\>Convert to Curve \</emph\>icon into a straight line or you change a curve with the mouse so that a point lies on the straight line, it is removed. The angle from which the point reduction is to take place \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Drawing - Grid\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Draw - Grid\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialog box\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Presentation - Grid\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress - Grid\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialog box\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>is 15° by default.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3155385\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziereliminatepoints.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155385\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	ga	Eliminate Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
