helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154646				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ControlCodes\"\>Shows nonprinting characters in your text, such as paragraph marks, line breaks, tab stops, and spaces.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145410				0	ga	When you delete a paragraph mark, the paragraph that is merged takes on the formatting of the paragraph that the cursor is in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147511				0	ga	To specify which nonprinting characters are displayed, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want in the \<emph\>Display of\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Hidden Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
