helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Edit Concordance File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148768				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>editing; concordance files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>concordance files; definition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	ga	Edit Concordance File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_CREATE_AUTOMARK\"\>Create or edit a list of words to include in an Alphabetical Index.\</ahelp\> A concordance file lists words that should be referenced in an alphabetical index, together with the page number(s) where they appear in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id837427				0	ga	You can use the Find All button on the Find & Replace dialog to highlight all places where a word appears, then open the Insert Index Entry dialog to add that word and places to the alphabetical index. However, if you need the same set of alphabetical indexes in multiple documents, the concordance file allows to enter every word just once, then use the list many times.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154645				0	ga	To access the Edit Concordance File dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149292				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables - Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	21			0	ga	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box, select "Alphabetical Index".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154107	22			0	ga	In the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Concordance file\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>File\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	24			0	ga	A concordance file contains the following fields: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152953				0	ga	"Search term" refers to the index entry that you want to mark in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	ga	"Alternative entry" refers to the index entry that you want to appear in the index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194				0	ga	The 1st and 2nd Keys are parent index entries. The "Search term" or the "Alternative entry" appears as a subentry under the 1st and 2nd Keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184				0	ga	"Match case" means that uppercase and lowercase letters are considered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282				0	ga	"Word only" searches for the term as a single word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220				0	ga	To enable the "Match case" or "Word only" options, click in the corresponding cell, and then select the check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153629				0	ga	To create a concordance file without the Edit Concordance File dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153644				0	ga	Use the following format guidelines when you create a concordance file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152770				0	ga	Each entry in the concordance file is on a separate line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	ga	Commented lines start with #.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153354				0	ga	Use the following format for the entries:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172				0	ga	Search term;Alternative entry;1st key;2nd key;Match case;Word only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3156270				0	ga	The entries "Match case" and "Word only" are interpreted as "No" or FALSE if they are empty or zero (0). All other contents are interpreted as "Yes" or TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	ga	For example, to include the word "Boston" in your alphabetical index under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line in the concordance file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	ga	Boston;Boston;Cities;;0;0 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151383				0	ga	This also finds "Boston" if it is written in lowercase letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	ga	To include the "Beacon Hill" district in Boston under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3150116	18			0	ga	Beacon Hill;Boston;Cities; 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Web Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
