helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154506				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>moving;objects and frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects and frames, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154506				0	ga	Resizing and Moving Frames, Objects With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	ga	You can resize and move selected frames and objects with the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	ga	To move a selected frame or object, press an arrow key. To move by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150762				0	ga	To resize a selected frame or object, first press Ctrl+Tab. Now one of the handles blinks to show that it is selected. To select another handle, press Ctrl+Tab again. Press an arrow key to resize the object by one grid unit. To resize by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	ga	The increment by which you move an object with the keyboard is determined by the document grid. To change the properties of the document grid, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01050100.xhp\" name=\"Text document - Grid\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Cross-references				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153641				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"Cross-references\"\>Cross-references\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	ga	\<variable id=\"reftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>This is where you insert the references or referenced fields into the current document. References are referenced fields within the same document or within sub-documents of a master document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197				0	ga	The advantage of entering a cross-reference as a field is that you do not have to adjust the references manually every time you change the document. Just update the fields with F9 and the references in the document are updated too.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id4333628				0	ga	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id4516129				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the Selection list, and then click Insert.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3151380				0	ga	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	ga	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	ga	Socraigh Tagairt				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	ga	Set target for a referenced field. Under \<emph\>Name\</emph\>, enter a name for the reference. When inserting the reference, the name will then appear as an identification in the list box \<emph\>Selection\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149556				0	ga	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For the target in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"insert a bookmark\"\>insert a bookmark\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150548				0	ga	Ionsáigh Tagairt				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147746				0	ga	Inserting a reference to another position in the document. The corresponding text position has to be defined with "Set Reference" first. Otherwise, inserting a reference by choosing a field name under \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146344				0	ga	In master documents, you can also reference from one sub-document to another. Note that the reference name will not appear in the selection field and has to be entered "by hand".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847				0	ga	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For referenced fields in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020400.xhp\" name=\"insert a hyperlink\"\>insert a hyperlink\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2408825				0	ga	Ceannteidil				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id9988402				0	ga	The Selection box shows a list of all headings in the order of their appearance in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6401257				0	ga	Ailt Uimhrithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5841242				0	ga	The Selection box shows a list of all numbered headings and numbered paragraphs in the order of their appearance in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id306711				0	ga	Bookmarks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150907				0	ga	After inserting a bookmark in the document with \<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>, the bookmarks entry on the \<emph\>References\</emph\> tab becomes usable. Bookmarks are used to mark certain text passages in a document. In a text document, you can use the bookmarks, for example, to jump from one passage in the document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155080				0	ga	In an HTML document, these bookmarks become anchors <A name>, which determine the target of hyperlinks for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011072				0	ga	Footnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011049				0	ga	If your documents contains a footnote, you can select the Footnotes entry. A reference to a footnote returns the footnote number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6794030				0	ga	(Inserted objects with captions)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7096774				0	ga	You can set references to objects that have captions applied. For example, insert a picture, right-click the picture, choose Caption. Now the object shows up as a numbered "Illustration" in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154772				0	ga	References are fields. To remove a reference, delete the field. If you set a longer text as a reference and you do not want to reenter it after deleting the reference, select the text and copy it to the clipboard. You can then reinsert it as "unformatted text" at the same position using the command \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>. The text remains intact while the reference is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id5824152				0	ga	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7374187				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, select a format in the "Insert reference to" list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7729728				0	ga	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2171086				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, click the format that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154333				0	ga	Insert reference to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148786				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_REF:LB_REFFORMAT\"\>Select the format that you want to use for the selected reference field.\</ahelp\> The following formats are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7576525				0	ga	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id641193				0	ga	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150039				0	ga	Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	ga	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150681				0	ga	Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154040				0	ga	Inserts the complete reference target text. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	ga	Thuas/Thíos				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	ga	Inserts "above" or "below", depending on the location of the reference target relative to the position of the reference field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	ga	As Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	ga	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target using the format specified in the page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5699942				0	ga	Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6420484				0	ga	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including superior levels depending on the context. See note below this table for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6986602				0	ga	Uimhir (gan chomhthéacs)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id616779				0	ga	Inserts only the number of the heading or numbered paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id791039				0	ga	Uimhir (comhthéacs iomlán)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id1953489				0	ga	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including all superior levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154635				0	ga	Chapter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	ga	Inserts the number of the chapter containing the reference target.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	ga	Category and Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155356				0	ga	Inserts the category (caption type) and the number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	ga	Téacs na Foscríbhinne				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145105				0	ga	Inserts the caption label of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	ga	Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883				0	ga	Inserts the caption number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id757469				0	ga	The "Number" format inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph. The superior levels are included depending on the context, as necessary. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5189062				0	ga	For example, when you are in a chapter 1, subchapter 2, subpart 5, this may be numbered as 1.2.5. When you insert here a reference to text in the previous subpart "1.2.4" and you apply the "Number" format, then the reference will be shown as "4". If in this example the numbering is set to show more sublevels, the same reference will be shown as "2.4" or "1.2.4", depending on the setting. If you use the "Number (full context)" format, you will always see "1.2.4", no matter how the numbered paragraph is formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156242				0	ga	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_REF:ED_REFNAME\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\> To set a target, click "Set Reference" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, type a name in this box, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. To reference the new target, click the target name in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	17			0	ga	In a master document, targets that are in different sub-documents are not displayed in the\<emph\> Selection\</emph\> list. If you want to insert a reference to the target, you must type the path and the name in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802250745				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159216				0	ga	If you select text in the document, and then insert a reference, the selected text becomes the contents of the field that you insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6501968				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edit the value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
