helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5044099				0	ga	Default settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id626544				0	ga	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id292062				0	ga	The thin gray lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1361735				0	ga	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id82399				0	ga	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7144993				0	ga	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5528427				0	ga	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4194158				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id8221076\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.2209in\" height=\"0.2445in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8221076\"\>default icons for borders\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7253028				0	ga	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders and all inner lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9441206				0	ga	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7276833				0	ga	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5273293				0	ga	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5110019				0	ga	User defined settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1820734				0	ga	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7093111				0	ga	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3673818				0	ga	Line types				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2593768				0	ga	Íomhá				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2055421				0	ga	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9836115				0	ga	A black line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6485793				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id1237525\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1237525\"\>solid line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1454512				0	ga	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4618671				0	ga	A gray line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1239356				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id2688680\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_7.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2688680\"\>gray line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9474166				0	ga	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1545457				0	ga	A white line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1681875				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id7340617\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_8.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7340617\"\>white line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	ga	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5908688				0	ga	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5118564				0	ga	Select a single cell in a Writer table, then choose \<emph\>Table - Table properties - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id244758				0	ga	Select a thick line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	ga	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id542313				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id4273506\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4273506\"\>setting thick lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	ga	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5400860				0	ga	All lines that are shown in white in the preview will be removed from the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Emphasizing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasizing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>emphasizing text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	ga	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	ga	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	ga	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	ga	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ga	Select the text, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	ga	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	ga	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork Gallery icon on the Drawing bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155177				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; centering on pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>centering;text frames on pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; centering text on\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155177				0	ga	\<variable id=\"text_centervert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_centervert.xhp\" name=\"Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\"\>Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920				0	ga	Select the text that you want to center on the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152765				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>To page\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149844				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Size\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, set the dimensions of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Position\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select "Center" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Horizontal\</item\>               \<emph/\>and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Vertical\</item\>               \<emph/\>boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153410				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	ga	To hide the borders of the frame, select the frame, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame/Object\</item\>. Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Borders\</item\> tab, and then click in the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Set No Border\</item\> box in the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line Arrangement\</item\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	ga	To resize the frame, drag the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147406				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; complex formulas in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;formulas/mean values\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	ga	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\"\>Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	ga	You can use predefined functions in a formula, and then insert the result of the calculation into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	ga	For example, to calculate the mean value of three numbers, do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	ga	Click in the document where you want to insert the formula, and then press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	ga	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon, and choose "Mean" from the Statistical Functions list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	ga	Type the three numbers, separated by vertical slashes (|).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	ga	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>. The result is inserted as a field into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	ga	To edit the formula, double-click the field in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Calculating in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149909				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;in Writer tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	ga	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	ga	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	ga	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	ga	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=10000/12\</item\>, and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	ga	You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\>         \<emph/\>icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	ga	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text frames from printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	ga	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	ga	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	ga	To Insert a Text Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	ga	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	ga	To Edit a Text Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	ga	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	ga	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	ga	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	ga	To Hide Text From Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	ga	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	ga	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	ga	To Link Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	ga	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	ga	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	ga	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Frame\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link Frames\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	ga	Click the frame that you want to link to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	ga	You can only link frames if:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	ga	The target frame is empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	ga	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	ga	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	ga	The source frame does not have a next link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	ga	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	ga	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	ga	The AutoSize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
