helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	bm_id8186284				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>rulers;using rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>horizontal rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indents; setting on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page margins on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;adjusting the width on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting page margins and cell widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ga	\<variable id=\"ruler\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\"\>Using Rulers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067D				0	ga	To show or hide rulers, choose \<emph\>View - Ruler\</emph\>. To show the vertical ruler, choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Writer - View\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>\</link\>, and then select \<emph\>Vertical ruler\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Ruler\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	ga	Adjusting Page Margins				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3155175				0	ga	The margins of a page are indicated by the filled areas at the ends of the rulers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149038				0	ga	Changing Indents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631				0	ga	Indents are adjusted with the three small triangles on the horizontal ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	26			0	ga	To change the left or the right paragraph indent, select the paragraph(s) that you want change the indent for, drag the bottom left or the bottom right triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	ga	To change the first line indent of a selected paragraph, drag the top left triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ga	You can also double-click anywhere on the horizontal ruler, and adjust the indents in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Inserting Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154922				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting pictures in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154922				0	ga	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149695				0	ga	There are several ways to insert a graphic object in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Calculating Cell Totals in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147400				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;sums in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>totals in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>table cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sums of table cell series\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147400				0	ga	\<variable id=\"calculate_intable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Cell Totals in Tables\"\>Calculating the Sum of a Series of Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Table\</emph\>, and insert a table with one column and more than one row into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154203				0	ga	Type a number in each cell of the column, but leave the last cell in the column empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	ga	Place the cursor in the last cell of the column, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sum\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table Bar\</item\>.\<br/\>The\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\> appears with the entry "=sum".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147775				0	ga	Click in the first cell of the series you want to sum up, drag to the final cell, and then release.\<br/\>$[officename] inserts a formula for calculating the sum of the values in the current column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	8			0	ga	Press Enter, or click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> in the Formula bar. \<br/\>The sum of the values in the current column is entered in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	ga	If you enter a different number anywhere in the column, the sum is updated as soon as you click in the last column cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	ga	Similarly, you can also quickly calculate the sum of a row of numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
