helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875				0	ga	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584				0	ga	You can design a page layout and then create a page style based on it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245				0	ga	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	ga	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	ga	Type a name for the page in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	ga	Double-click the name in the list to apply the style to the current page. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	ga	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page break\</item\> and then select “Default” from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	ga	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom page style with a different header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
