helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150101				0	ga	\<variable id=\"numbering_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_lines.xhp\" name=\"Adding Line Numbers\"\>Adding Line Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	ga	$[officename] can insert line numbers in an entire document or to selected paragraphs in your document. Line numbers are included when you print your document. You can specify the line numbering interval, the starting line number, and whether to count blank lines or lines in frames. You can also add a separator between line numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	ga	Line numbers are not available in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153410				0	ga	To Add Line Numbers to an Entire Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	ga	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156241				0	ga	To Add Line Numbers to Specific Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3156264				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153385				0	ga	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	ga	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	ga	Right-click the "Default" paragraph style and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150222				0	ga	All paragraph styles are based on the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150956				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151077				0	ga	Select the paragraph(s) where you want to add the line numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151096				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	ga	Select \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153758				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3146864				0	ga	You can also create a paragraph style that includes line numbering, and apply it to the paragraphs that you want to add line numbers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146880				0	ga	To Specify the Starting Line Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	ga	Click in a paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150721				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	ga	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148414				0	ga	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Restart at the paragraph\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	ga	Enter a line number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start with\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153804				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153934				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06180000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Line Numbering\"\>Tools - Line Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Numbering\"\>Format - Paragraph - Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id2212591				0	ga	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Finding and Replacing in Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id1163670				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>finding; text/text formats/styles/objects\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>replacing; text and text formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>styles;finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>text formats; finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formats; finding and replacing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>objects;finding by Navigator\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Asian languages;search options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	ga	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	ga	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id6226081				0	ga	The Find & Replace dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	ga	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialog without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	ga	To Find Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	ga	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	ga	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	ga	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	ga	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	ga	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	ga	When you click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a character style to all at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id5891598				0	ga	To Replace Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	ga	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	ga	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	ga	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	ga	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	ga	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	ga	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	ga	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	ga	To Find Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	ga	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	ga	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	ga	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	ga	Check \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for Styles\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	ga	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3231299				0	ga	To Find Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	ga	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	ga	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	ga	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	ga	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	ga	More options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	ga	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	ga	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for English text.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	ga	When you have enabled Asian language support under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialog offers options to search Asian text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2489394				0	ga	The Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	ga	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	ga	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	ga	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	ga	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or find the next text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Indexes Covering Several Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;multiple documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	ga	\<variable id=\"indices_multidoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_multidoc.xhp\" name=\"Indexes Covering Several Documents\"\>Indexes Covering Several Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	ga	There are several ways to create an index that spans several documents:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ga	Create an \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index in each individual document\"\>index in each individual document\</link\>, copy and paste the indexes into a single document, and then edit them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147118				0	ga	Select each index, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>\</link\>, and then enter a name for the index. In a separate document, choose\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>), and then locate and insert a named index section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	ga	Create a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\>, add as subdocuments the files that you want to include in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Inserting Page Numbers in Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155624				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>footers; with page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; numbers and count of\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page numbers; footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering;pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155624				0	ga	\<variable id=\"footer_pagenumber\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_pagenumber.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\"\>Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id8230842				0	ga	You can easily insert a page number field in the footer of your document. You can also add a page count to the footer, for example, in the form "Page 9 of 12"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id7867366				0	ga	To Insert a Page Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3153155				0	ga	If you want, you can align the page number field as you would text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id2988677				0	ga	To Additionally Add a Page Count				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	ga	Click in front of the page number field, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> and enter a space; click after the field, enter a space and then type \<item type=\"literal\"\>of\</item\> and enter another space.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>running titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>floating titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers; chapter information\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	ga	\<variable id=\"header_with_chapter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_chapter.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\"\>Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	ga	Before you can insert chapter information into a header or footer, you must first set the outline numbering options for the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244				0	ga	To Create a Paragraph Style for Chapter Titles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155874				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	ga	Select the numbering style for the chapter titles in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, for example, "1,2,3...".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150219				0	ga	Type "Chapter" followed by a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150245				0	ga	Enter a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>After\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150505				0	ga	To Insert the Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527				0	ga	Apply the paragraph style that you defined for chapter titles to the chapter headings in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>               \<emph/\>or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153762				0	ga	Click in the header or footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146863				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\> and click the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Document\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153175				0	ga	Click "Chapter" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list and "Chapter number and name" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147065				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147095				0	ga	The header on every page that uses the current page style automatically displays the chapter name and number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159260				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>text; navigating and selecting with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>navigating; in text, with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;text, with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard; navigating and selecting in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159260				0	ga	\<variable id=\"text_nav_keyb\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_nav_keyb.xhp\" name=\"Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard\"\>Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	ga	You can navigate through a document and make selections with the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id1031200810571916				0	ga	To move the cursor, press the key or key combination given in the following table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id1031200810571929				0	ga	To select the characters under the moving cursor, additionally hold down the Shift key when you move the cursor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	ga	Key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155870				0	ga	Feidhm				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156220	25			0	ga	                  \<emph\>+\</emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>Command key\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Ctrl key\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ga	Right, left arrow keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	ga	Moves the cursor one character to the left or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	ga	Moves the cursor one word to the left or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149629				0	ga	Up, down arrow keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	ga	Moves the cursor up or down one line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	ga	(\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>) Moves the current paragraph up or down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149624				0	ga	Home				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the current line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149586				0	ga	Home				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156237				0	ga	In a table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the contents in the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the contents of the current cell. Press again to move the cursor to the first cell in the table. Press again to move the cursor to the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154410				0	ga	End				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the end of the current line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154235				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the end of the document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	ga	End				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154850				0	ga	In a table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	ga	Moves to the end of the contents in the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155894				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the end of the contents of the current cell. Press again to move the cursor to the last cell in the table. Press again to move the cursor to the end of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155944				0	ga	PgUp				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148678				0	ga	Scrolls up one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148701				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149998				0	ga	PgDn				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153018				0	ga	Scroll down one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	ga	Moves the cursor to the footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Inserting Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	ga	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	ga	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	ga	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	ga	Cross-Referencing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	ga	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	ga	To Insert a Target				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	ga	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list, select “Set Reference”.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	ga	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	ga	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>. The name of the target is added to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Selection\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	ga	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	ga	To Create a Cross-Reference to a Target				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7032074				0	ga	Position the cursor in the text where you want to insert a cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7796868				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\> to open the dialog, if it is not open already.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	ga	Cross-Referencing an Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	ga	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	ga	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	ga	Updating Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	ga	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7321390				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\> to switch between viewing the reference names and the reference contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blank pages with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>empty page with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; even/odd pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	ga	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3155876\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_designerdialog.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155876\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	ga	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id8194219				0	ga	To Set Up Alternating Page Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	ga	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	ga	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	ga	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	ga	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	ga	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	ga	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	ga	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	ga	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	ga	To Suppress the Printout of Empty Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	ga	If two even or two odd pages directly follow each other in your document, Writer will insert an empty page by default. You can suppress those automatically generated empty pages from printing and from exporting to PDF.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
