helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151178				0	ga	\<variable id=\"insert_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_line.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Horizontal Line\"\>Inserting a Horizontal Line\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2165898				0	ga	This guide is about inserting graphical rules. You can also insert other lines, see \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/line_intext.xhp\"\>Drawing Lines in Text\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3149691				0	ga	Click in the document where you want to insert the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Horizontal Rule\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	83			0	ga	Click the line that you want to insert in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id5338602				0	ga	The "Plain" type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5342265				0	ga	If you select the "Plain" type of rules, an empty paragraph is inserted at the position of the cursor. This paragraph has the style "Horizontal Line", with a line as the lower border of the paragraph. You can edit that Paragraph Style to change the properties of all "Plain" rules in your document. For example you can set the left indent to 3 inches, or you can change the line style, thickness, and color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id707113				0	ga	To edit the "Plain" rule style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5267494				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> to open the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5074922				0	ga	In the listbox at the bottom, select to display "All Styles".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8491470				0	ga	Right-click the "Horizontal Line" paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3253883				0	ga	Choose Modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3196203				0	ga	For example, open the Borders tab page to set the thickness and style of the lines. Open the Indents & Spacing tab page to set the indents of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8385265				0	ga	The graphical type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2582476				0	ga	Select any rule type below of the "Plain" rule type. This inserts a new paragraph at the position of the cursor. A picture showing a graphical horizontal line is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150217				0	ga	The inserted line is anchored to the current paragraph and centered between the page margins.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2111575				0	ga	To edit the graphical line, right-click the line and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150231				0	ga	You can also insert one of these lines by dragging it from the \<emph\>Rulers\</emph\> folder in the \<emph\>Gallery\</emph\> into the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
