helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147682				0	ga	\<variable id=\"chapter_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Outline Numbering\"\>Outline Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155605				0	ga	You can modify the heading hierarchy or assign a level in the hierarchy to a custom paragraph style. You can also add chapter and section numbering to heading paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading 1" paragraph style is at the top of the outline hierarchy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155626				0	ga	To Add Automatic Numbering to a Heading Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the heading style that you want to add chapter numbers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	ga	In the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> box, select the numbering style that you want to use, and then click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CE				0	ga	To Remove Automatic Outline Numbering From a Heading Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
