helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Defining Borders for Objects 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146957				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>objects; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; for objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; around objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>charts;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;object borders\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	ga	\<variable id=\"border_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/border_object.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Objects\"\>Defining Borders for Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	ga	In Writer, you can define borders around OLE objects, plug-ins, diagrams/charts, graphics and frames. The name of the menu to be used depends on the object selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	ga	To Set a Predefined Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	ga	Select the object for which you want to define a border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	4			0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	ga	Click one of the predefined border styles. This replaces the current border style of the object with the selected style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152474				0	ga	To Set a Customized Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	ga	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344	9			0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - (object name) – Borders\</item\>.\<br/\>Replace (object name) with the actual name of the object type you selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	ga	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ga	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3125865				0	ga	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	ga	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to Contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Positioning Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147828				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>objects;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>positioning;objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>anchors;options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>centering;images on HTML pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828				0	ga	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251				0	ga	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599				0	ga	Anchoring				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	ga	Effect				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650				0	ga	Mar charachtar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181				0	ga	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	ga	To center an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then center the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	ga	To character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235				0	ga	Anchors the selected item to a character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071				0	ga	Go halt				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	ga	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122				0	ga	Go leathanach				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	ga	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	ga	Go fráma				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697				0	ga	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715				0	ga	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\>         \<emph/\>submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145078				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering; changing the level of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>levels;changing outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowering outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rising outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;outline levels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
