helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	ga	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab, type a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	ga	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	ga	Use the tabs in the dialog to set the layout options for the page style, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154851				0	ga	To Apply a Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	ga	Click in the page that you want to apply the page style to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Style\</item\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ga	Double-click a name in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
