helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id413830				0	ga	\<variable id=\"pagenumbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>Page Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	ga	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id6091494				0	ga	To Insert Page Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\> to insert a page number at the current cursor position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	ga	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	ga	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</item\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	ga	To Start With a Defined Page Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	ga	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	ga	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	ga	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	ga	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	ga	To Format the Page Number Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	ga	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	ga	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	ga	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	ga	Using Different Page Number Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	ga	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	ga	In Writer, you will need different page styles. The first page style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following page style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	ga	Both page styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	ga	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the page style has a different "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	ga	For example, the "First Page" page style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify\</item\> from the context menu. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab, you can see the "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	ga	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	ga	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	ga	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	ga	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between page styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	ga	To Apply a Different Page Style to the First Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	ga	Click into the first page of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	ga	Double-click the "First Page" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	ga	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	ga	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" page atyle only, or insert footers in both page styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5298318				0	ga	To Apply a Manually Inserted Page Style Change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	ga	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different page style will be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>. You see the \<emph\>Insert Break\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list box, select a page style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	ga	The selected page style will be used from the current paragraph to the next page break with style. You may need to create the new page style first.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Animating Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151182				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>text animation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>effects; text animation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>animations;text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151182				0	ga	\<variable id=\"text_animation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_animation.xhp\" name=\"Animating Text\"\>Animating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	ga	You can only animate text that is contained in a drawing object, such as rectangles, lines, or text objects. For example, draw a rectangle, then double-click the rectangle and enter your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	ga	Select the drawing object containing the text that you want to animate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Object - Text Attributes\</item\>, and then click the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Animation\</item\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Effect\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the animation that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	ga	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id7693411				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F0				0	ga	\<variable id=\"table_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_select.xhp\"\>Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	ga	You can select a table in a text document with a keyboard or with a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	ga	To select a table with the keyboard, move the cursor into the table, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all the cells are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	ga	To select a table with the mouse, move the mouse pointer to a position just above and left of the table. The mouse pointer becomes a diagonal arrow. Click to select the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	ga	To select a row or column with the mouse, point to a position just left of the row or above the column. The mouse pointer becomes an arrow. Click to select the row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Calculating Across Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154248				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; across multiple text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating across\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154248				0	ga	\<variable id=\"calculate_multitable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_multitable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Across Tables\"\>Calculating Across Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	ga	You can perform calculations that span across more than one table in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795				0	ga	Open a text document, insert two tables, and type numbers in a few cells in both tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147815				0	ga	Place your cursor in an empty cell in one of the tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833				0	ga	Press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	ga	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	ga	Click in a cell containing a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274				0	ga	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
