helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152999				0	ga	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_fromchart\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\"\>Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155890				0	ga	You can insert a copy of a chart that is not updated when you modify the chart data in the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	ga	Open the text document that you want to copy the chart to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	ga	Open the spreadsheet containing the chart that you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	ga	In the spreadsheet, click the chart. Eight handles appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	ga	Drag the chart from the spreadsheet to the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	ga	You can resize and move the chart in the text document as you would any object. To edit the chart data, double-click the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
