helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	bm_id6609088				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;paper trays\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper tray selection\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155909				0	ga	\<variable id=\"printer_tray\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/printer_tray.xhp\" name=\"Selecting printer paper trays\"\>Selecting Printer Paper Trays\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	ga	Use page styles to specify different paper sources for different pages in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	ga	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\>               \<emph/\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	ga	Right-click the page style in the list that you want to specify the paper source for, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
