helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154307				0	ga	Press Enter to switch to edit mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_EDITMODE\"\>Allows you to immediately edit the selected cell after pressing the Enter key.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ga	Expand formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400	11			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_FORMAT\"\>Specifies whether to automatically apply the formatting attributes of the selected cell to the empty adjacent cells.\</ahelp\> If, for example, the contents of the selected cell have the bold attribute, this bold attribute will also apply to adjacent cells. Cells that already have a special format will not be modified by this function. You can see the range in question by pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> + * (multiplication sign on the number pad) shortcut. This format also applies to all new values inserted within this range. The normal default settings apply to cells outside this range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451				0	ga	Expand references when new columns/rows are inserted				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_EXPREF\"\>Specifies whether to expand references when inserting columns or rows adjacent to the reference range. This is only possible if the reference range, where the column or row is inserted, originally spanned at least two cells in the desired direction.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	ga	\<emph\>Example:\</emph\> If the range A1:B1 is referenced in a formula and you insert a new column after column B, the reference is expanded to A1:C1. If the range A1:B1 is referenced and a new row is inserted under row 1, the reference is not expanded, since there is only a single cell in the vertical direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	ga	If you insert rows or columns in the middle of a reference area, the reference is always expanded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176				0	ga	Highlight selection in column/row headings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
