helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the type of record that you want to create. $[officename] inserts a number in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> column of the record that corresponds to the type that you select here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a short name for the record. The short name appears in the \<emph\>Identifier\</emph\> column in the list of records.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155994				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter additional information for the selected record. If you want, you can also enter the information in the corresponding field in the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163716				0	ga	Finding and Filtering Records				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478				0	ga	You can search for records by matching a keyword to a field entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159181				0	ga	Entering Search key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159125	11			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/query\"\>Type the information that you want to search for, and then press Enter. To change the filter options for the search, long-click the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> icon, and then select a different data field. You can use wildcards such as % or * for any number of characters, and _ or ? for one character in your search. To display all of the records in the table, clear this box, and then press Enter. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
