helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149991				0	ga	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	8			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_RB_AS_FIELD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as fields.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\> to insert the selected data into the document as fields. These \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090006.xhp\" name=\"database fields\"\>database fields\</link\> work as wildcards for the individual database columns and can be used for form letters. Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Data to Fields\"\>\<emph\>Data to Fields\</emph\>\</link\> icon to match the contents of the fields to the currently selected record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	ga	If several records are selected when you choose the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> function, the mail merge fields will be inserted according to the number of records. Also, a field command such as "Next record" will be inserted automatically between individual field command blocks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	ga	The \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog lets you define which database fields to insert into the document and how to format the paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	ga	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> area, use the arrow button to select the database table columns into which you want to insert field contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	ga	Database columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	ga	Lists all columns of the database table, which can be accepted in the selection list box to insert them into the document. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_TXT_DB_COLUMN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database columns that you want to insert it in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ga	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_TOEDIT\"\>Moves the fields that you selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box into the selection field.\</ahelp\> You can also double-click the entry to select it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166411				0	ga	Select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_ED_DB_TEXT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Lists the database columns that you selected to be inserted into the document. You can also enter text here. This text will be also inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> The entries' order in the selection field corresponds to the data order in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153257				0	ga	Stíl Ailt				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	ga	By default, the inserted paragraphs are formatted with the current Paragraph Styles. This format corresponds to the "none" entry in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> list box. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_DB_PARA_COLL\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This is where you can select other Paragraph Styles to apply to the paragraph you want to insert into the document.\</ahelp\> The list box displays the available Paragraph Styles defined in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> and managed in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Style Catalog\"\>Style Catalog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	ga	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	ga	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372				0	ga	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined date/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	ga	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616				0	ga	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	ga	Ionsáigh Colún				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	ga	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827				0	ga	Replace with				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	ga	Scrios Colún				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	ga	Colún				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	ga	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539				0	ga	Hide Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	ga	Taispeáin colúin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	ga	Tuilleadh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl (Mac: Command) key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	ga	Uile				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349				0	ga	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	ga	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the previous control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062				0	ga	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	ga	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	ga	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to select the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657				0	ga	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	ga	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	ga	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	ga	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	ga	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>date fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	ga	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	ga	When you enter a year using two digits, the corresponding four digit value is determined by a setting in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\>. For example, if 1935 is set as the lower limiting value and you enter 34 as a date value, then the result is 2034 instead of 1934.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	ga	The pre-set limit value will be saved for each document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
