helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148643				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>controls; events\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>events; controls\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>macros; assigning to events in forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148643				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170103.xhp\" name=\"Events\"\>Events\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152350	2			0	ga	On the\<emph\> Events \</emph\>tab page you can link macros to events that occur in a form's control fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	ga	When the event occurs, the linked macro will be called. To assign a macro to an event, press the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. An \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060700.xhp\" name=\"Assign Macro\"\>Assign Macro\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>dialog\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149732				0	ga	Depending on the control, different events are available. Only the available events for the selected control and context are listed on the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab page. The following events are defined:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149191				0	ga	Ceadaigh an gníomh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEACTIONPERFORMED\"\>This event takes place before an action is triggered by clicking the control.\</ahelp\> For example, clicking a "Submit" button initiates a send action; however, the actual "send" process is started only when the \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> event occurs. The \<emph\>Approve action\</emph\> event allows you to kill the process. If the linked method sends back FALSE, \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> will not be executed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	ga	Rith an gníomh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ACTIONPERFORMED\"\>The \<emph\>Execute action\</emph\> event occurs when an action is started.\</ahelp\> For example, if you have a "Submit" button in your form, the send process represents the action to be initiated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156343				0	ga	Athraithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148755	42			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_CHANGED\"\>The\<emph\> Changed \</emph\>event takes place when the control loses the focus and the content of the control has changed since it lost the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153524				0	ga	Téacs mionathraithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
