helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ga	In the data source explorer you see the data sources registered in $[officename] with their queries and tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ga	\<emph\>Establishing a connection\</emph\> - As soon as you select an individual table or query, a connection to the data source is established. Once the connection is opened, the name of the data source, the Queries or Tables entry, and the name of the query or table selected is shown in bold type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Closes the connection to the data source. See \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Connections\</emph\> in the Options dialog box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151379				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>To rename an entry, call this command and enter the new name. You can also do this by selecting the entry and pressing F2. The database must support renaming, otherwise this command is not enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id273445				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the selected database file for editing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
