helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	2			0	ga	This \<emph\>General \</emph\>tab enables you to define the general properties of a form control. These properties differ, depending on the control type. Not all of the following properties are available for every control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155342				0	ga	If you export the current form document to HTML format, the default control values are exported, not the current control values. Default values are determined - depending on the type of control - by the properties' Default value (for example, in text fields), Default status (for check boxes and option fields), and Default selection (for list boxes).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149734				0	ga	Cumasaithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ENABLED\"\>If a control field has the property "Enabled" (Yes), the form user will be able to use the control field.\</ahelp\> If the property is disabled, it will not be enabled (No) and will be displayed in a gray color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153320				0	ga	Líon na línte				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235	75			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LINECOUNT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. This setting is only active if you chose "Yes" in the "Dropdown" option.\</ahelp\>For combo boxes with the Dropdown property, you can specify how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. With control fields which do not have the Dropdown option, the line's display will be specified by the size of the control field and the font size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
