helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1154E				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies if a Push Button behaves as a Toggle Button. If you set Toggle to "Yes", you can switch between the "selected" and "not selected" control states when you click the button or press the spacebar while the the control has the focus. A button in the "selected" state appears "pressed in".\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11558				0	ga	Tóg Fócas ar Chlic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1156E				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you set this option to "Yes", the Push Button receives the focus when you click the button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11578				0	ga	Folaigh an roghnúchán				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1158E				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"37965\"\>Specifies whether a text selection on a control remains selected when a the focus is no longer on a control.\</ahelp\> If you set \<emph\>Hide selection\</emph\> to "No", the selected text remains selected when the focus is no longer on the control that contains the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11598				0	ga	Stíl				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115AE				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"37966\"\>Specifies whether Check boxes and Option buttons are displayed in a 3D look (default) or a flat look.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B8				0	ga	Dath na himlíne				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115CE				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"37967\"\>Specifies the border color for controls that have the Border property set to "flat".\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B7				0	ga	Symbol color				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115BB				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the color for symbols on controls, for example the arrows on a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149314				0	ga	Date min				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155755	132			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152866				0	ga	Value min				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147505	134			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can determine here a value for the control field to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields you can determine a minimum value to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153298				0	ga	Time min				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831	136			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155746				0	ga	Cruinneas deachúlach				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096	138			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DECIMAL_ACCURACY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151340				0	ga	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	10			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>On the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> tab page, this option specifies the name for the control field. On the \<emph\>Form Properties \</emph\>tab page, this option specifies the name for the form.\</ahelp\>Each control field and each form has a \<emph\>Name \</emph\>property through which it can be identified. The name will appear in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\> and, using the name, the control field can be referred to from a macro. The default settings already specify a name which is constructed from using the field's label and number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	ga	If you work with macros, make sure that the names of the controls are unique.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146325				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>controls; grouping\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>groups;of controls\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>forms; grouping controls\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	ga	The name is also used to group different controls that belong together functionally, such as radio buttons. To do so, give the same name to all members of the group: controls with identical names form a group. Grouped controls can be represented visually by using a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Group Box\"\>Group Box\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149720				0	ga	Navigation bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918	198			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATIONBAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of the table control.\</ahelp\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of table controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158426				0	ga	Read-only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153215	43			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_READONLY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the control is read-only (Yes) or if it can be edited (No).\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Read-only \</emph\>property can be assigned to all controls in which the user can enter text. If you assign the read-only property to an image field which uses graphics from a database, the user will not be able to insert new graphics into the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912				0	ga	Imlíne				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637	140			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BORDER\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the field's border should be displayed "Without frame", with a "3-D look" or "Flat".\</ahelp\>With control fields that have a frame, you can determine the border display on the form using the \<emph\>Border \</emph\>property. You can select among the "Without frame", "3-D look" or "Flat" options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149266				0	ga	Tab order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147483				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABINDEX\"\>The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property determines the order in which the controls are focused in the form when you press the Tab key.\</ahelp\> In a form that contains more than one control, the focus moves to the next control when you press the Tab key. You can specify the order in which the focus changes with an index under \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156207				0	ga	The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property is not available to \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Controls\"\>Hidden Controls\</link\>. If you want, you can also set this property for image buttons and image controls, so that you can select these controls with the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150378				0	ga	When creating a form, an index is automatically assigned to the control fields that are added to this form; every control field added is assigned an index increased by 1. If you change the index of a control, the indices of the other controls are updated automatically. Elements that cannot be focused (Tabstop = No) are also assigned a value. However, these controls are skipped when using the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	ga	You can also easily define the indices of the different controls in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0509200912114423				0	ga	Scrollú an rotha luiche				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200912114566				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets whether the value changes when the user scrolls a mouse wheel. Never: No change of the value. When focused: (default) The value changes when the control has the focus and the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled. Always: The value changes when the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled, no matter which control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154049				0	ga	Stádas réamhshocraithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150837				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_CHECKED\"\>Specifies whether an option or a check box is selected by default.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149242				0	ga	For a reset type button, you can define the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156266				0	ga	For grouped option fields, the status of the group corresponding to the default setting is defined by the \<emph\>Default Status\</emph\> property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156150				0	ga	Roghnú réamhshocraithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148730	37			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SELECT_SEQ\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.\</ahelp\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028	203			0	ga	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default selection\</emph\> entry defines the status of the list box if the reset button is activated by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id919217				0	ga	For a List box that contains a value list, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id50050				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog, select the entries that you want to mark as selected when you open the form that contains the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
