helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200920593851				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines whether the control will be visible in live mode. In design mode, the control is always visible.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154683				0	ga	Note that if this property is set to "Yes" (the default), this does not necessarily mean the control will really appear on the screen. Additional constraints are applied when calculating a control's effective visibility. For instance, a control placed in a hidden section in Writer will never be visible at all, until at least the section itself becomes visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154691				0	ga	If the property is set to "No", then the control will always be hidden in live mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154614				0	ga	Older OpenOffice.org versions up to 3.1 will silently ignore this property when reading documents which make use of it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
