helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	ga	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ga	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234				0	ga	Restrict Files to Display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	ga	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id4651326				0	ga	Cursor Position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id5509201				0	ga	In general, all documents open with the cursor at the start of the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id6594744				0	ga	One exception appears when the author of a Writer text document saves and reopens a document: The cursor will be at the same position where it has been when the document was saved. This only works when the name of the author was entered in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3422650				0	ga	Press Shift+F5 to set the cursor to the last saved position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453				0	ga	Opening an Empty Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar or choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>. This opens a document of the document type specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	ga	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501358				0	ga	System File Dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME Dialogs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501356				0	ga	On most operating systems, you can choose to use the system file dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME dialogs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501429				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\> to switch the type of open/save dialogs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501449				0	ga	The %PRODUCTNAME dialogs support file download and upload using secure https connections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501453				0	ga	Opening Files from a Web Server				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	ga	You can enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialogs. The URL must start with file:/// or ftp:// or http://. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501548				0	ga	If you use the %PRODUCTNAME dialog, you can use the https:// prefix for a secure connection, and you can save a document on the web server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	ga	When you open a file by a URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens a local copy of the file in the system's temp folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Recording and Displaying Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes example\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Track Changes, see review function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	ga	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	ga	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	ga	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ga	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	ga	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	ga	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ga	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Sending Documents as E-mail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153345				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>documents; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>e-mail attachments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attachments in e-mails\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	ga	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	ga	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	ga	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Internet - E-mail\</emph\> in the Options dialog box.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	ga	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3595385				0	ga	In case you want to send the e-mail to a recipient who only has software that cannot read the OpenDocument format, you can send the current document in an often used proprietary format.\<br/\>For a text document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Word\</item\>. For a spreadsheet, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Excel\</item\>. And for a presentation, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft PowerPoint\</item\>. \<br/\>If you want to send the document as a read-only file, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as PDF\</item\>.\<br/\>These commands do not change your current document. Only a temporary copy is created and sent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Changing the Title of a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>titles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;document titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; changing titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	ga	\<variable id=\"change_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/change_title.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Title of a Document\"\>Changing the Title of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	ga	You can specify a title for your document. Some file manager utilities can display the titles next to the filenames of your documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	ga	How to change the title of the current document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Properties of\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	ga	Type the new title in the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100000.xhp\" name=\"Properties of\"\>Properties of\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>loading;XML files\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>file filters;XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	ga	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	ga	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	ga	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	ga	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	ga	 \<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	ga	 \<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	ga	 \<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	ga	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	ga	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id5569017				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing XML filters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id6426892				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating and Testing XML filters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Inserting Hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	ga	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	ga	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	ga	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	ga	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	ga	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	ga	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	ga	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	ga	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	ga	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	ga	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ga	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Turning off Automatic URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognizing URLs automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic hyperlink formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;turning off URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>predictive text, see also AutoCorrect function/AutoFill function/AutoInput function/word completion/text completion\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	ga	\<variable id=\"autocorr_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autocorr_url.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\"\>Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	ga	When you enter text, $[officename] automatically recognizes a word that may be a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\> and replaces the word with a hyperlink. $[officename] formats the hyperlink with direct font attributes (color and underline) the properties of which are obtained from certain Character Styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	ga	If you do not want $[officename] to automatically recognize URLs as you are typing, there are several ways of turning off this feature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306				0	ga	Undo URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	ga	When you are typing and notice that a text has just been automatically converted into a hyperlink, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z to undo this formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	ga	If you do not notice this conversion until later, select the hyperlink and choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152350				0	ga	Turn off URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	ga	Load a document of the type for which you want to modify the URL recognition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	ga	If you want to modify the URL recognition for text documents, open a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	ga	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	ga	If you unmark \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>, words will no longer be automatically replaced with hyperlinks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	ga	In $[officename] Writer there are two check boxes in front of \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>. The box in the first column is for later post-editing and the box in the second column is for AutoCorrect as you type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Executing SQL Commands				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>SQL; executing SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>queries;creating in SQL view\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>commands;SQL\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>executing SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	ga	\<variable id=\"data_enter_sql\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_enter_sql.xhp\" name=\"Executing SQL Commands\"\>Executing SQL Commands\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ga	With the help of SQL commands you can control the database directly, and can also create and edit tables and queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	ga	Not all database types support all SQL instructions. If necessary, find out which SQL commands are supported by your database system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id9577929				0	ga	To execute an SQL statement directly				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id7923825				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open a database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id9448530				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Tools - SQL\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176	91			0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Create Query in SQL View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154071\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbnewquerysql.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	92			0	ga	Select an existing query from the list and click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156212\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbqueryedit.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156212\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Query\</emph\> window, choose \<emph\>View - Switch Design View On/Off\</emph\>. Edit the SQL command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460	96			0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Run\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3152886\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbanativesql.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152886\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The result of the query is displayed in the upper window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298	98			0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> or \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153159\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153159\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to save the query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
