helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ga	If you drag objects out of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navigator.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>\<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>\</link\>, you can specify in the submenu of the Navigator's \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon whether to copy the object, insert it as a link or insert it as a hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	ga	You can cancel a drag-and-drop operation in $[officename] at any time by pressing the Esc key before releasing the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>opening;documents on WebDAV server\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	ga	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	ga	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	ga	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	ga	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	ga	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	ga	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	ga	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	ga	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	ga	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	ga	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	ga	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	ga	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	ga	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	ga	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	ga	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If you enable \<emph\>Remember password till end of session\</emph\>, your password will be remembered for subsequent WebDAV connections until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	ga	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id2182378				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>About digital signatures\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Error Report Tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>reports;error reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	ga	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ga	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ga	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	ga	Starting the Error Report Tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	ga	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046				0	ga	Completing the Report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	ga	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	ga	Tuairisc Earráide á seoladh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	ga	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	ga	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	ga	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	ga	What Data is Sent?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ga	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	ga	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Undoing Direct Formatting for a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	bm_id6606036				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>undoing;direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;undoing all\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;all direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes;undoing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;undoing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>restoring;default formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067F				0	ga	\<variable id=\"undo_formatting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/undo_formatting.xhp\"\>Undoing Direct Formatting for a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	ga	You can undo all formatting that has not been made by styles in a few steps.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	ga	Removing all Direct Formatting in a $[officename] Writer Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063F				0	ga	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+A\</item\> to select the whole text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064A				0	ga	Removing all Direct Formatting in a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	ga	While pressing the Shift key click the first and then the last sheet tab to select all sheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	ga	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+A\</item\> to select the whole text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F0				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ga	Removing all Direct Formatting in a $[officename] Presentation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Outline\</emph\> tab to open outline view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_id3906674				0	ga	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+A\</item\> to select the whole text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B0				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01011000.xhp\"\>Undo Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>spadmin\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; adding, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default printer; UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard printer under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes; fax programs/fax printers under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; faxes under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PostScript; PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converters; PostScript, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF; PostScript to PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834				0	ga	\<variable id=\"spadmin\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\" name=\"Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\"\>Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159876				0	ga	%PRODUCTNAME uses the installed fonts of your system. In a text document you can select from all printable fonts. In an HTML document or in Web layout, only fonts that are visible on screen are offered. In spreadsheets and drawings you can select from all installed fonts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ga	Under UNIX based platforms, the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> is provided to help you set up printers and faxes for use with the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ga	Call the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	ga	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ga	Enter: ./spadmin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	ga	After it starts, the window of the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	ga	Following a server installation, the system administrator first logs on as with root privileges, and starts the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>. The administrator then creates a general printer configuration file called {install_path}/share/psprint/psprint.conf for all users. All changes are immediately available to all users.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177				0	ga	Setting up Printers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	ga	Under UNIX based platforms, the $[officename] software only offers direct support for printers using the PostScript technology. Other printers must be set up as described in the section \<emph\>Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software\</emph\>. The $[officename] software automatically provides a printer with the default driver for each system queue. You can add additional printers as needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564				0	ga	Adding a Printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	ga	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	ga	Enter: ./spadmin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Create Printer\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ga	Select the appropriate driver for your printer. If you are not using a PostScript printer or your model is not listed, use the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> driver or follow the steps below. You can also add new drivers using the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> button or delete unnecessary drivers using the \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	ga	Choose a command line that you can use to print on your printer (for example, lp -d my_queue). Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	ga	Give the printer a name and determine whether it should become the default printer. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	ga	To print a test page, click on \<emph\>Test Page\</emph\>. If the test page fails to print or is incorrectly printed, check all settings as described in \<emph\>Changing Printer Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147				0	ga	Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	ga	When installing a non-PostScript printer, you must set your system so that PostScript can be converted into the language of the printer. We recommend using current PostScript conversion software such as Ghostscript (http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~ghost/).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154639				0	ga	You should set up the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> in that case. Also make sure that the page margins are set correctly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	ga	If you are using a printer using the PostScript technology, you should install a description file for the printer (PostScript Printer Definition - PPD) so that you can utilize the specific printer features like paper tray selection, duplex print function and all built-in fonts. You can also use the generic printer driver since it contains the most important data and is suitable for most printers. In that case, you will have to do without the paper tray selection and must correctly set the page margins.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	128			0	ga	Some PPD files are installed as default files. If there is no matching PPD file for your printer, you will find various PPD files at http://www.adobe.com/products/printerdrivers/. You can also ask the manufacturer of your printer for PPD files. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435				0	ga	Importing Drivers When Creating a New Printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Import\</emph\> in the driver selection dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	347			0	ga	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> to select the directory where you unpacked the PPD files. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Selection of drivers\</emph\> list box, select the printer driver you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	ga	Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152885				0	ga	Deleting Drivers When Creating a New Printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	ga	Select the printer driver.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149909				0	ga	Be sure that you do not delete the generic printer driver, and remember that drivers deleted from server installations are no longer available to other users who are using the same server installation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	ga	If the printer has more fonts built in than the usual PostScript fonts, you must also load the AFM files for these additional fonts. Copy the AFM files into the {install_path}/share/psprint/fontmetric directory or into the {install_path}/user/psprint/fontmetric directory. You can find AFM files, for example, at ftp://ftp.adobe.com/pub/adobe/type/win/all/afmfiles/.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148388				0	ga	Changing Printer Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	ga	In the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>, select the printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog appears containing several tab pages. This is where you can make settings that are used according to the PPD file of the selected printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833				0	ga	Select the command on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. You can remove superfluous commands using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Paper\</emph\> tab page, you can define the paper format and paper tray to be used as the default settings for this printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "grayscale" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, otherwise choose "color". If switching to grayscale leads to unfavorable results, you can also select "color" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colors are described as well as the PostScript level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	ga	The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	ga	You should also set the page margins correctly on the \<emph\>Additional settings\</emph\> tab when using the generic printer driver so that your printout is not cropped. You can also enter a description in the Comments field, which will also be displayed on the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	ga	Some of these settings can also be set for the current printout in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog or the \<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\> dialog in the $[officename] software with the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	ga	Renaming or Deleting Printers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	ga	Select a printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	ga	To rename the selected printer, click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>. Enter an appropriate name in the dialog that appears and click OK. The name must be unique and should be chosen so that you can recognize the printer and the application. Printer names must be assigned the same for all users because, when documents are exchanged, the selected printer remains unchanged if the recipient has it under the same name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	ga	To delete the selected printer, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>. The default printer or a printer that has been created by the system administrator in a server installation cannot be removed using this dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Selecting a Default Printer \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	ga	To make the printer selected from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box the default printer, double-click its name or click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154204				0	ga	Using Fax Functionality				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463				0	ga	If you have installed a fax package such as Efax or HylaFax on your computer, you can send faxes with the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575				0	ga	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	ga	Enter: ./spadmin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808				0	ga	Click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151070				0	ga	Select \<emph\>Connect a fax device\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787				0	ga	Choose whether to use the default driver or another printer driver. If you are not using the default driver, select the appropriate driver. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	ga	Enter a command line with which to communicate with the fax in the following dialog. In the command line of each fax sent "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(PHONE)" by the telephone number of the recipient fax machine. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is transmitted in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	ga	Assign a name to your new fax printer and determine whether the telephone numbers (see below) marked in the text should be removed from the printout, or not. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	ga	You can now send faxes by printing to the printer that has just been created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148419				0	ga	Enter the fax number as text in the document. You can also enter a field that takes the fax number from your active database. In any case, the fax number must start with the characters @@# and end with @@. A valid entry would have the form @@#1234567@@.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826				0	ga	If these characters including the telephone number are not printed, activate the \<emph\>Fax number is removed from the printout\</emph\> option under \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. If no telephone number is entered in the document, a dialog prompting you for it will appear after the printout.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	ga	In $[officename] you can also activate an icon for sending faxes to a default fax. To do this, choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Toolbars\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> and add from "Documents" the \<emph\>Send Default Fax\</emph\> icon. You can set which fax is used when this button is pressed under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	ga	Remember to create one separate print job for each fax, otherwise, the first recipient will receive all the faxes. In the \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge\</emph\> dialog select the \<emph\>Printer\</emph\> option and then select the \<emph\>Single print jobs\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146929				0	ga	Connecting a PostScript to PDF Converter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154989				0	ga	If a PostScript to PDF converter such as Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is installed on your computer, you can quickly create PDF documents in the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524				0	ga	In spadmin, click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	ga	Select \<emph\>Connect a PDF converter\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	ga	Choose whether to use the default driver, the Acrobat Distiller driver or another driver. The driver "Generic Printer (T42 enabled)" prefers the type 42 fonts over type 3 fonts; this driver is a good choice for output to a software PostScript interpreter. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155128				0	ga	In the next dialog, enter a command line for the PostScript->PDF Converter. Enter the directory where the PDF files should be saved. If you do not provide a directory, the user's home directory will be used. In the command line "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(OUTFILE)" by the target file, the name of which is created from the document name. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the Postscript code is forwarded in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. If Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is in the search path, you can use one of the predefined command lines. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	ga	Assign a name to your new PDF converter. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	ga	You can now create PDF documents by printing to the converter that has just been created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Selecting the Document Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id3083278				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>languages; selecting for text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>character styles;language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drawings; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults;languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; default languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dictionaries, see also languages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083278				0	ga	\<variable id=\"language_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Document Language\"\>Selecting the Document Language\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	ga	The language you select for your document determines the dictionary used for spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation, the decimal and thousands delimiter used and the default currency format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	ga	The language you select applies to the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	ga	Within the document, you can apply a separate language to any paragraph style. This has priority over the language of the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	ga	You can assign a language to selected pieces of text in a paragraph, either by direct formatting or with a character style. This assignment has priority over the paragraph style and document language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	ga	Selecting a language for the whole document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\>. Go to \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>\<emph\>Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ga	Under \<emph\>Default languages for documents\</emph\>, select the document language for all newly created documents. If you mark \<emph\>For the current document only\</emph\>, your choice will only apply to the current document. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152938				0	ga	Selecting a language for a Paragraph Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	ga	Place the cursor in the paragraph whose paragraph style you want to edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	ga	Open the context menu and select \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	ga	All paragraphs formatted with the current paragraph style will have the selected language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	ga	Applying a language directly to selected text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	ga	Select the text to which you want to apply a language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3159348				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164				0	ga	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and proceed accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	ga	Selecting a language for a Character Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	ga	Open the Styles and Formatting window and click on the \<emph\>Character Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	ga	Click on the name of the character style to which you want to apply a different language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150753				0	ga	Then open the context menu in the Styles and Formatting window and select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character Style\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150321				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	ga	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	ga	Now you can apply the character style to your selected text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id8703268				0	ga	Adding More Text Languages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7919248				0	ga	Dictionaries are supplied and installed as extensions. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Language - More Dictionaries Online\</item\> to open the dictionaries page in your default web browser.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id5174108				0	ga	Select a dictionary in the list of descriptions. Click the heading in a dictionary description that you want to get.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2897427				0	ga	In the next page, click the Get It icon to download the dictionary extension. Note the folder name to which your browser downloads the file. Download additional dictionaries as you like.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3906979				0	ga	In %PRODUCTNAME, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> and click Add to install the downloaded extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id0220200911174493				0	ga	After you installed the extensions, you should close %PRODUCTNAME (including the Quickstarter), and restart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9100924				0	ga	Setting UI Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	ga	A standard installation of %PRODUCTNAME software will give you a user interface (UI) of your chosen language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	ga	Most users download the American English version, which gives you English menu commands and English application help. If you want another language for the menus (and for the application help, if available in that language), change the UI language as follows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	ga	Select another UI language in the "User interface" listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	ga	Click OK and restart the OpenOffice.org software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	ga	If the listbox doesn't list the language that you want, see "Adding More UI Languages".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	ga	Adding More UI Languages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ga	Open your Web browser and enter \<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\"\>http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ga	Select and download the correct language pack for your version of %PRODUCTNAME software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ga	Close %PRODUCTNAME software (also close the Quickstarter, if you enabled it).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	ga	Install the language pack. Either double-click the exe file, or unpack the tar.gz file according to standard practice on your platform.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152483				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Font\"\>Format - Character - Font\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Printing in Black and White				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150125				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>printing; black and white\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>black and white printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors; not printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; printing in black\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150125				0	ga	\<variable id=\"print_blackwhite\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_blackwhite.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Black and White\"\>Printing in Black and White\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	ga	Printing text and graphics in black and white				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. The \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	ga	Click on \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. This opens the Properties dialog for your printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	ga	Select the option to print in black and white. For further information, refer to the user's manual of your printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ga	Confirm the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ga	The current document will be printed in black and white.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	ga	Printing in black and white in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	ga	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw, as appropriate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	ga	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	ga	Under \<emph\>Quality,\</emph\> select either \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> or \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	ga	When either of these options is selected, all presentations or drawings will be printed without color. If you only want to print in black for the \<emph\>current\</emph\> print job, select the option in \<emph\>File - Print - %PRODUCTNAME Draw/Impress\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149786	15			0	ga	               \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> converts all colors to a maximum of 256 gradations from black to white. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	16			0	ga	               \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> converts all colors into the two values black and white. All borders around objects are printed black. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ga	Printing only text in black and white				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	ga	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer you can choose to print color-formatted text in black and white. You can specify this either for all subsequent text documents to be printed, or only for the current printing process.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	ga	Printing all text documents with black and white text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ga	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer/Web.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	ga	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910	22			0	ga	Under \<emph\>Contents,\</emph\> mark \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	ga	All text documents or HTML documents will be printed with black text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920				0	ga	Printing the current text document with black and white text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. Then click the \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Print text in black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing dialogs\"\>Printing dialogs\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154146				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options dialog\"\>Tools - Options dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>databases; text formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables in text format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; spreadsheets to text format\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154824				0	ga	\<variable id=\"data_dbase2office\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_dbase2office.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ga	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBASE import and export, you can use a common text format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	ga	Importing Data into $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ga	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	ga	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	ga	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	ga	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	ga	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ga	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBASE format in the folder of a dBASE database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBASE" and the folder of the dBASE database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	ga	Exporting in CSV Text Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ga	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	ga	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	ga	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Merging Versions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>documents; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions;merging document versions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	ga	\<variable id=\"redlining_docmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging Versions\"\>Merging Versions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	ga	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	ga	When a document has been edited by more than one person, it is possible to merge the edited copies into the original. The only requirement is that the documents differ only and exclusively in the recorded changes - all other original text must be identical.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425				0	ga	Open the original document into which you want to merge all copies.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Merge Document\</emph\>. A file selection dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	ga	Select the copy of the document from the dialog. If there have been no subsequent changes to the original document, the copy is merged into the original.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ga	If changes have been made to the original document, an error dialog appears that informs you that the merge is unsuccessful.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	ga	After you merge the documents you will see the recorded changes from the copy in the original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Collaboration				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id130008				0	ga	\<variable id=\"collab\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/collab.xhp\"\>Collaboration\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5821710				0	ga	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, Impress, and Draw, only one user at a time can open any document for writing. In Calc, many users can open the same spreadsheet for writing at the same time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9590136				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Share Document dialog where you can enable or disable collaborative sharing of the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2519913				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable to share the current document with other users. Disable to use the document unshared. This will invalidate the not yet saved edits that other users applied in the time since you last opened or saved this document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id6917020				0	ga	Collaboration in Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6799218				0	ga	Some commands are not available (grayed out) when change tracking or document sharing is activated. For a new spreadsheet you cannot apply or insert the grayed out elements. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id3274941				0	ga	Creating a new spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9804681				0	ga	User A creates a new spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2109744				0	ga	The user does not want to share the spreadsheet for collaboration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5374614				0	ga	User A opens, edits, and saves the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id768761				0	ga	The user wants to share the document for collaboration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6844691				0	ga	The user chooses \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> to activate the collaboration features for this document. A dialog opens where the user can choose to enable or disable sharing. If the user enables sharing, the document will be saved in shared mode, which is also shown on the title bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5288857				0	ga	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> command can be used to switch the mode for the current document from unshared mode to shared mode. If you want to use a shared document in unshared mode, you would save the shared document using another name or path. This creates a copy of the spreadsheet that is not shared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id8842127				0	ga	Opening a spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7276528				0	ga	User A opens a spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id8363902				0	ga	The spreadsheet document is not in shared mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	ga	The user can open, edit, and save the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5323343				0	ga	The spreadsheet document is in shared mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5824457				0	ga	The user sees a message that the document is in shared mode and that some features are not available in this mode. The user can disable this message for the future. After clicking OK, the document is opened in shared mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5800653				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the same contents are changed by different users, the Resolve Conflicts dialog opens. For each conflict, decide which changes to keep.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6263924				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps your change, voids the other change.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id3609118				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the change of the other user, voids your change.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7184057				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps all your changes, voids all other changes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id786767				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the changes of all other users, voids your changes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2934965				0	ga	Saving a shared spreadsheet document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1174657				0	ga	User A saves a shared document. The following conditions can apply:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2577593				0	ga	The document was not modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5883968				0	ga	The document is saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9049653				0	ga	The document was modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1976683				0	ga	If the changes do not conflict, the document is saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id43946				0	ga	If the changes conflict, the Resolve Conflicts dialog will be shown. User A must decide for the conflicts which version to keep, "Keep Mine" or "Keep Other". When all conflicts are resolved, the document is saved. While user A resolves the conflicts, no other user is able to save the shared document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6449171				0	ga	Another user tries to save the shared document and resolves conflicts in this moment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7101046				0	ga	User A sees a message that a merge-in is in progress. User A can choose to cancel the save command for now, or retry saving some time later.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7186498				0	ga	When a user successfully saves a shared spreadsheet, the document will be reloaded after the save command, so that the spreadsheet shows the latest version of all changes that got saved by all users. A message shows that "foreign changes have been added" when another user did change some contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2871791				0	ga	Collaboration in Writer, Impress, and Draw				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2675862				0	ga	For all modules Writer, Impress, Draw, and for Calc when document sharing is not enabled, a file locking is possible. This file locking is available even when accessing the same document from different operating systems:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7333597				0	ga	User A opens a document. The following conditions can apply:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9976195				0	ga	The document is not locked by any other user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2507400				0	ga	This document will be opened for read and write access by user A. The document will be locked for other users until user A closes the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id216681				0	ga	The document is marked as "read-only" by the file system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7709585				0	ga	This document will be opened in read-only mode. Editing is not allowed. User A can save the document using another document name or another path. User A can edit this copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4309518				0	ga	The document is locked by another user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id206610				0	ga	User A sees a dialog that tells the user the document is locked. The dialog offers to open the document in read-only mode, or to open a copy for editing, or to cancel the Open command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id29349651				0	ga	User access permissions and sharing documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id11746571				0	ga	Some conditions must be met on operating systems with a user permission management.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id25775931				0	ga	The shared file needs to reside in a location which is accessible by all collaborators.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id90496531				0	ga	The file permissions for both the document and the corresponding lock file need to be set so that all collaborators can create, delete, and change the files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id71864981				0	ga	Write access also enables other users to (accidentally or deliberately) delete or change a file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
