helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153662				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;complex text layout languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>languages;complex text layout\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;CTL languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text layout for special languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-to-left text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text from right to left\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bi-directional writing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hindi;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hebrew;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Arabic;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Thai;entering text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	ga	\<variable id=\"ctl\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ctl.xhp\" name=\"Languages Using Complex Text Layout\"\>Languages Using Complex Text Layout\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	ga	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420				0	ga	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	ga	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+D or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Right Shift Key - switch to right-to-left text entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+A or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Left Shift Key - switch to left-to-right text entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	ga	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ga	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	ga	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ga	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	ga	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809				0	ga	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150300.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\"\>Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Dearadh Tábla				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155448				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; creating in design view (manually)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields in databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fields;database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoValue (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>primary keys;design view\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	ga	\<variable id=\"data_tabledefine\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\" name=\"Table Design\"\>Table Design\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	ga	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	ga	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	ga	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	ga	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id1595507				0	ga	Include a "primary key" data field. Base needs a primary key to be able to edit the table contents. A primary key has unique contents for each data record. For example, insert a numerical field, right-click the first column, and choose \<emph\>Primary Key\</emph\> from the context menu. Set \<emph\>AutoValue\</emph\> to "Yes", so Base can automatically increment the value for each new record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ga	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	ga	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBASE III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	ga	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	ga	Airíonna Réimse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	ga	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	ga	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Accepting or Rejecting Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150247				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>changes; accepting or rejecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;accepting or rejecting changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150247				0	ga	\<variable id=\"redlining_accept\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_accept.xhp\" name=\"Accepting or Rejecting Changes\"\>Accepting or Rejecting Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	ga	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1110200810120034				0	ga	In Writer text documents you can also accept or reject changes by choosing commands from the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	ga	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ga	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ga	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	ga	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ga	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	ga	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	ga	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Saving Documents Automatically				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152924				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;documents, automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backups;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155536				0	ga	\<variable id=\"doc_autosave\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_autosave.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents Automatically\"\>Saving Documents Automatically\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	ga	To create a backup file every time you save a document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	ga	Mark \<emph\>Always create backup copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797	6			0	ga	If the \<emph\>Always create backup copy\</emph\> option is selected, the old version of the file is saved to the backup directory whenever you save the current version of the file. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ga	You can change the backup directory by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>, then change the \<emph\>Backups\</emph\> path in the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	ga	The backup copy has the same name as the document, but the extension is .BAK. If the backup folder already contains such a file, it will be overwritten without warning.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149514				0	ga	To save recovery information automatically every n minutes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	ga	Mark \<emph\>Save AutoRecovery information every\</emph\> and select the time interval.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	ga	This command saves the information necessary to restore the current document in case of a crash. Additionally, in case of a crash %PRODUCTNAME tries automatically to save AutoRecovery information for all open documents, if possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
