helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations, see pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarization filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aging filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterizing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136				0	ga	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	ga	Inserting Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	ga	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	ga	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	ga	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	ga	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	ga	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	ga	Editing Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id187078				0	ga	Icons on the Picture bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	ga	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ga	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	ga	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>Graphic \<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	ga	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	ga	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	ga	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id2572405				0	ga	The Picture dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id6457411				0	ga	Right-click the picture and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> from the submenu to open a properties dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7991882				0	ga	Change the properties of the selected picture, then click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574				0	ga	Saving Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	ga	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803544667				0	ga	To export a bitmap in Draw or Impress:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	ga	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3157139				0	ga	The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> command writes the picture with all applied filter effects to a file. The \<emph\>Save as Picture\</emph\> command in the context menu saves the picture without any filter effects, if the picture was inserted as a linked picture. An embedded picture will always be saved or exported with filters applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ga	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	ga	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874				0	ga	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	ga	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803525078				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To export a bitmap in Writer: Right-click the bitmap, choose Save Graphics. You see the Graphics Export dialog. Enter a file name and select a file type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id1033051				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\"\>Graphic Filter Bar from the Picture Bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	ga	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	ga	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	ga	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	ga	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	ga	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	ga	Select one of the options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	ga	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	ga	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	ga	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	ga	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	ga	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	ga	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	ga	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Relative and Absolute Links				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>absolute hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks, see also links\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	ga	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_rel_abs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp\" name=\"Relative and Absolute Links\"\>Relative and Absolute Links\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ga	When you include hyperlinks, two factors must be taken into account: whether they are set as relative or absolute on saving, and whether or not the file is present.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ga	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>\<emph\>Load/Save - General\</emph\>\</link\> and specify in the \<emph\>Save URLs relative to\</emph\> field if $[officename] creates \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#speichern\" name=\"relative or absolute hyperlinks\"\>relative or absolute hyperlinks\</link\>. Relative linking is only possible when the document you are working on and the link destination are on the same drive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	ga	You should create the same directory structure on your hard disk as that which exists in the web space hosted by your Internet provider. Call the root directory for the homepage on your hard disk "homepage", for example. The start file is then "index.html", the full path being "C:\\homepage\\index.html" (assuming Windows operating system). The URL on your Internet provider's server might then be as follows: "http://www.myprovider.com/mypage/index.html". With relative addressing, you indicate the link relative to the location of the output document. For example, if you placed all the graphics for your homepage in a subfolder called "C:\\homepage\\images", you would need to give the following path to access the graphic "picture.gif": "images\\picture.gif". This is the relative path, starting from the location of the file "index.html". On the provider's server, you would place the picture in the folder "mypage/images". When you transfer the document "index.html" to the provider's server through the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> dialog, and if you have marked the option \<emph\>Copy local graphics to Internet\</emph\> under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>, $[officename] will automatically copy the graphic to the correct directory on the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	ga	An absolute path such as "C:\\homepage\\graphics\\picture.gif" would no longer function on the provider server. Neither a server nor the computer of a reader needs to have a C hard drive: operating systems such as Unix or MacOS do not recognize drive letters, and even if the folder homepage\\graphics existed, your picture would not be available. It is better to use relative addressing for file links.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	ga	A link to a web page, for example, "www.example.com" or "www.myprovider.com/mypage/index.html" is an absolute link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	ga	$[officename] also reacts differently, depending on whether the file referred to in the link exists, and where it is located. $[officename] checks every new link and sets a target and protocol automatically. The result can be seen in the generated HTML code after saving the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145317				0	ga	The following rules apply: A relative reference ("graphic/picture.gif") is only possible when both files exist on the same drive. If the files are on different drives in your local file system, the absolute reference follows the "file:" protocol ("file:///data1/xyz/picture.gif"). If the files are on different servers or if the target of the link is not available, the absolute reference uses the "http:" protocol ("http://data2/abc/picture.gif").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	ga	Be sure to organize all files for your homepage on the same drive as the start file of the homepage. In this way, $[officename] can set the protocol and target so that the reference on the server is always correct.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897				0	ga	When you rest your mouse on a hyperlink, a help tip displays the absolute reference, since $[officename] uses absolute path names internally. The complete path and address can only be seen when you view the result of the HTML export, by loading the HTML file as "Text" or opening it with a text editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Searching Tables and Form Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	bm_id4066896				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>finding;records in form documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;finding records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;tables and forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
