helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	ga	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	ga	To Add a Button to a Document 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ga	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	ga	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
