helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	ga	Open the Gallery by clicking the \<emph\>Gallery\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar, or by selecting \<emph\>Tools - Gallery\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	ga	Select a theme.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617				0	ga	Select an object by a single click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443				0	ga	Drag the object on to the other object in the document while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Using the Filter Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150322				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>filters; Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filter conditions;connecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	ga	\<variable id=\"filternavigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/filternavigator.xhp\"\>Using the Filter Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3150322				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterNavigator\"\>To connect several filter conditions with Boolean OR, click the \<emph\>Filter navigation\</emph\> icon on the filter bar.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> window appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FILTER_NAVIGATOR\"\>The filter conditions that have been set appear in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. As soon as a filter is set, you see a blank filter entry at the bottom of the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> . You can select this entry by clicking the word "Or". Once you have selected the blank filter entry, you can enter additional filter conditions in the form. These conditions are linked by Boolean OR to the previously defined conditions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620				0	ga	The context menu can be called for each entry in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_FILTER_IS_NOT_NULL\"\>You can edit the filter conditions in this area directly as text. If you wish to check if a field has content or no content, you can select the filter conditions "empty" (SQL:"Is Null") or "not empty" (SQL: "Is not Null").\</ahelp\> It is also possible to delete the entry by using the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374				0	ga	You can move filter conditions in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> by dragging and dropping, or use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Down Arrow. To copy filter conditions, drag them while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Integrating new UNO components				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>add-ons, see UNO components\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>UNO components;integrating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;UNO components\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	ga	\<variable id=\"integratinguno\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"Integrating new UNO components\"\>Integrating new UNO components\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	ga	Programmers can write and integrate their own UNO (Universal Network Objects) components to $[officename]. Those new components can be added to the $[officename] menus and toolbars; we call them "Add-Ons".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ga	The integration of new components is supported by some tools and services. Details can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide. The three main steps are as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	3			0	ga	Register the new components within $[officename]. This can be accomplished using the tool \<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg\</item\>, which can be found in {installpath}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>/ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\\\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ga	Integrate the new components as services. The ProtocolHandler and JobDispatch services assist you; more information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ga	Change the user interface (menus or toolbars). This can be done almost automatically by writing an XML text file that describes the changes. More information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ga	The Add-Ons can extend the functionality of $[officename]. They are not related to the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Add-Ins\"\>Add-Ins\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Add-Ins\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> that provide new functions for $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Applying Line Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153884				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>separator lines; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reference lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arrows; defining arrow lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line styles; applying\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884				0	ga	\<variable id=\"linestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/linestyles.xhp\" name=\"Applying Line Styles Using the Toolbar\"\>Applying Line Styles Using the Toolbar\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	ga	The \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> toolbar contains icons and combo boxes to define various line attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	6			0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144510\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144510\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id5858221\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_lineendstyle.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5858221\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to select an arrow style for the right and left ends of a line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	ga	Select a style from the \<emph\>Line Style\</emph\> box and specify the width in the \<emph\>Line Width\</emph\> box. A width of 0 corresponds to 1 pixel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	ga	Select the line and arrow color in the \<emph\>Line Color\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Searching for Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	bm_id5681020				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>fonts;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding; attributes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;Find & Replace mode\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	ga	\<variable id=\"find_attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/find_attributes.xhp\"\>Searching for Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	ga	You can search for text with attributes that are applied either by direct formatting or by styles. For example, if you search for the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> attribute, all instances of text that do not use the default font are found. All text that has a directly coded font attribute, and all text where a style switches the font attribute, are found.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	ga	If you want to find text with any font by name, click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog of %PRODUCTNAME Writer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	ga	After you select the attributes that you want to search for, the \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\> box in the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area of the %PRODUCTNAME Writer \<emph\>Find & Replace \</emph\>dialog changes to \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	ga	If you want to search for text in which attributes were set by using direct formatting and styles, select the \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	ga	The search criteria for attributes are listed below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	ga	To search for all font changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	ga	Clear the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box if necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> check box, and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog, you now can read "Font" below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FB				0	ga	All places where a font change was applied, either directly or by assigning an appropriate style, are found.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FE				0	ga	To reset the Find & Replace mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	ga	To stop searching for the current attributes, reset the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog to normal mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	ga	Click \<emph\>No Format\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id6837672				0	ga	Searching for attributes is available in the Find & Replace dialog for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Creating Reports 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	bm_id3729667				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;reports\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	ga	\<variable id=\"data_reports\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_reports.xhp\"\>Creating Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	ga	A report is a Writer text document that can show your data in an organized order and formatting. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, you have a choice to create a report either manually using drag-and-drop in the Report Builder window, or semi-automatic by following a series of dialogs in the Report Wizard. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4094363				0	ga	The following list gives you some information to decide which method to use for your data:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8514358				0	ga	Report Builder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9764091				0	ga	Treoraí Tuairisce				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1579638				0	ga	Started by "Create Report in Design View" command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1886959				0	ga	Started by "Use Wizard to Create Report" command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id455030				0	ga	Full flexibility to use report headers and footers, page headers and footers, multi-column reports.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8409985				0	ga	Uses a Writer template to generate a report document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5931272				0	ga	Use drag-and-drop to position the record fields or other design elements like pictures or lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
