helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3139133				0	ga	Different methods exist to start a chart:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6772972				0	ga	Insert a chart based on data from cells in Calc or Writer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6049684				0	ga	These charts update automatically when the source data changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2356944				0	ga	Insert a chart with a default data set, and then use the Data Table dialog to enter your own data for that chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id866115				0	ga	These charts can be created in Writer, Impress and Draw. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146763				0	ga	Copy a chart from Calc or Writer into another document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id701315				0	ga	These charts are snapshots of the data at the time of copying. They do not change when the source data changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4439832				0	ga	In Calc, a chart is an object on a sheet, it cannot be a sheet of its own.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
