helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	ga	%PRODUCTNAME stores the information about the created reports in the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	ga	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ga	Double-click one of the report names to open the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	ga	These links are added automatically when you create a new report by the Report Wizard or in the Report Builder window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id1695608				0	ga	Editing a Report Created in the Report Builder Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id7510910				0	ga	Right-click the name of a report in the database file window, then choose Edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id8138065				0	ga	The Report Builder window opens with the report's information loaded. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id5086825				0	ga	Use the toolbars and menu commands and drag-and-drop to edit the report as stated in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id4747154				0	ga	Execute the report to see the resulting report document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153104				0	ga	Editing a Report Created by the Report Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	ga	On the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100500.xhp\" name=\"last dialog page of the Report AutoPilot\"\>last dialog page of the Report Wizard\</link\>, you can choose to edit the report template before you use the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	ga	You can edit the page styles for the first page and the following pages of the report as well as the paragraph styles, the number formats, the printed field labels, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D7				0	ga	Unless you have a thorough understanding of the database the report accesses, do not edit the SQL statement, database name, the hidden form controls, or the related information on the report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Copying Graphics Between Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	ga	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	ga	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	ga	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	ga	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ga	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ga	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	ga	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	ga	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	ga	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	ga	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	ga	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	ga	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	ga	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	ga	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	ga	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	ga	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	ga	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	ga	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	ga	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	ga	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	ga	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	ga	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Adding Graphics to the Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Gallery; adding pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;adding to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures in Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	49			0	ga	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Adding Graphics to the Gallery\"\>Adding Graphics to the Gallery\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ga	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	ga	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ga	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	ga	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	ga	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	ga	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772				0	ga	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	ga	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	ga	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ga	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	ga	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	ga	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	ga	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Opening documents saved in other formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
