helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	ga	Click one of the predefined border styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	ga	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	ga	Setting a Customized Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	ga	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ga	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	ga	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	ga	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	ga	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ga	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Adding Texture to Chart Bars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>charts; bars with textures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>textures;on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;textures on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	ga	You can add texture to the bars in a graph or chart (instead of the default colors) via bitmap graphics:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ga	Enter edit mode by double-clicking on the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ga	In the context menu choose \<emph\>Object Properties\</emph\>. Then choose the \<emph\>Area\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	ga	Click on \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>. In the list box select a bitmap as a texture for the currently selected bars. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to accept the setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Working with Groups 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id6888027				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>groups;entering/exiting/ungrouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exiting;groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>marking, see selecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id2454298				0	ga	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/groups.xhp\"\>Working with Groups\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2307199				0	ga	You can combine several graphic objects into a group so that you can use them like a single object. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9983825				0	ga	You can move, transform, resize, distort, or convert all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group any time to change the individual objects. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	ga	You can change the properties (line size, fill color, and more) of all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group and change the individual objects. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	ga	Groups can also be nested to form groups within other groups. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7705618				0	ga	To group objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id607013				0	ga	Select the objects together that you want to group. Hold down Shift while you click the individual objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	ga	Right-click any of the selected objects to open the context menu. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	ga	In Impress or Draw, choose Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group – Group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6738792				0	ga	To select the objects, you can also drag a selection frame around the objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	ga	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	ga	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7424237				0	ga	To enter a group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	ga	Right-click any object of the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	ga	In Impress or Draw, choose Enter Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Edit Group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	ga	Now you can select and edit a single object in the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	ga	You can add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	ga	The objects that are not part of the group are shown with dimmed colors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id9141819				0	ga	To exit a group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	ga	Right-click any object of the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	ga	In Impress or Draw, choose Exit Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Exit Group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	ga	To exit a group in Draw or Impress, you can also double-click anywhere outside the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7889950				0	ga	To ungroup a group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	ga	Right-click any object of the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	ga	In Impress or Draw, choose Ungroup. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Ungroup.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	ga	Now you can select and edit all objects as individual objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
