helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	ga	\<variable id=\"data_forms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_forms.xhp\"\>Working with Forms\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	ga	Using forms, you can define how to present the data. Open a text document or a spreadsheet and insert the controls such as push buttons and list boxes. In the properties dialogs of the controls, you can define what data the forms should display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	ga	Creating a New Form With the Form Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	ga	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can create a new form using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01090000.xhp\"\>Form Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	ga	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	ga	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Form\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	ga	Creating a New Form Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	ga	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	ga	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Create Form in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ga	A new text document opens. Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls\</link\> to insert form controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10670				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon to access all forms that were created from within the current database window. In addition, you can use the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> icons to add database form controls to any Writer or Calc document, but these documents will not be listed in the database window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Printing Address Labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>labels; from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>stickers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases;creating labels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	ga	\<variable id=\"labels_database\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels_database.xhp\" name=\"Printing Address Labels\"\>Printing Address Labels\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	37			0	ga	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab page, select the format of the label sheets you want to print on. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370863				0	ga	Choose the database and table from which to get the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id013020090337089				0	ga	Select a database field of which you want to print the contents. Click the button that shows a left arrow to insert the database field into the Label Text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370930				0	ga	Continue to select and insert database fields if you want more fields on every label. You can press Enter to insert a new line, and you can type any character to insert fixed text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370924				0	ga	Optionally, if you want to type more text, apply formatting, or insert images and line art, you should enable \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. If you enable this, once you leave the Labels dialog box a small window opens with a Synchronize button. Now you only need to work on the first label on the labels document, then click the Synchronize button to copy your work to every label of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_idN10687				0	ga	Click \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ga	When you see the label document, you might want to temporarily enable \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Field Names\</item\>. This displays the fields in a more visible manner, so that you can arrange and edit label contents more easily.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148484				0	ga	You can save and/or print the label document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id8476821				0	ga	When you choose to print the document, you will be asked if you want to print a form letter. Answer Yes to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Mail Merge\</link\> dialog. In the Mail Merge dialog, you can select the records for which you want to print labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
