helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	ga	Non-breaking spaces				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	31			0	ga	To prevent two words from being separated at the end of a line, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and the Shift key when you type a space between the words.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	ga	In Calc, you cannot insert non-breaking spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	ga	Non-breaking dash				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	ga	An example of a non-breaking dash is a company name such as A-Z. Obviously you would not want A- to appear at the end of a line and Z at the beginning of the next line. To solve this problem, press Shift+Ctrl+ minus sign. In other words, hold down the Shift and Ctrl keys and press the minus key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802				0	ga	Hyphen, dash				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	66			0	ga	In order to enter longer dashes, you can find under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>\<emph\>- Options\</emph\> the \<emph\>Replace dashes\</emph\> option. This option replaces one or two minus signs under certain conditions with an en-dash or an em-dash (see \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	67			0	ga	For additional replacements see the replacements table under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Replace\"\>\<emph\>Replace\</emph\>\</link\>. Here you can, among other things, replace a shortcut automatically by a dash, even in another font.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	ga	Definite separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	60			0	ga	To support automatic hyphenation by entering a separator inside a word yourself, use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+minus sign. The word is separated at this position when it is at the end of the line, even if automatic hyphenation for this paragraph is switched off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special characters\"\>Special characters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Web Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156014				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/07/09000000.xhp\" name=\"Web Pages\"\>Web Pages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	ga	To create a new web page for the Internet, open a new \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	ga	A tool for creating new web pages is the Web Layout mode, which you enable with \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285				0	ga	Creating a New Web Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150808				0	ga	Switch to the web layout mode by choosing \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\> or by opening a new HTML document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	ga	To create an HTML page from your $[officename] document, save the page using one of the "HTML Document" file types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
