helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Queries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>queries;overview (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; printing queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries; printing (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02000000.xhp\" name=\"Queries\"\>Queries\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	ga	A "query" is a special view of a table. A query can display chosen records or chosen fields within records; it can also sort those records. A query can apply to one table to multiple tables, if they are linked by common data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	ga	Use queries to find records from data tables based on certain criteria. All queries created for a database are listed under the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> entry. Since this entry contains the database queries, it is also called the "query container".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153750				0	ga	Printing Queries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149183				0	ga	To print a query or table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	ga	Open a text document (or a spreadsheet document if you prefer the specific printing functions of this type of document).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	ga	Open the database file and click the Table icon if you want to print a table, or click the Query icon if you want to print a query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	ga	Drag the name of the table or query into the open text document or spreadsheet. The dialog \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Database Columns\"\>Insert Database Columns\</link\> opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	ga	Decide which columns = data fields you want to include. You can also click the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> button and select a corresponding formatting type. Close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	ga	The query or table will be inserted into your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	ga	Print the document by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153146				0	ga	You can also open the data source view (F4), select the entire database table in the data source view (button in the top left corner of the table), and then drag the selection to a text document or spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Sorting and Filtering Data\"\>Sorting and Filtering Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	ga	Allows you to sort and filter the data in a query table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	ga	With the \<emph\>Query Design\</emph\>, you can create and edit a query or view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Through Several Tables\"\>Query Through Several Tables\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	ga	The query result can contain data from several tables if these are linked to each other by suitable data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159149				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Formulating Query Criteria\"\>Formulating Query Criteria\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	ga	You can find out which operators and commands can be used to formulate the filter conditions for a query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Executing Functions\"\>Executing Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	ga	You can perform calculations with the data of a table and store the results as a query result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
