helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154146				0	ga	Delete cascade				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155309				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_REL_PROPERTIES_RB_CASC_DEL\"\>Specifies that all external key fields will be deleted if you delete the corresponding primary key field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140	22			0	ga	When you delete a primary key field with the\<emph\> Delete cascade \</emph\>option, all records from other tables that have this key as their foreign key are also deleted. Use this option with great care; it is possible that a major portion of the database can be deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ga	Set null				2002-02-02 02:02:02
