helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Loading Line and Arrow Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>line styles;loading\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;about line ends\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>arrows;loading arrow styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>loading;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	ga	\<variable id=\"line_arrow_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_arrow_styles.xhp\" name=\"Loading Line and Arrow Styles\"\>Loading Line and Arrow Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	ga	You can use styles to organize similar line and arrow types. $[officename] provides a few standard style files that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a style file, or even create a custom style file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154485				0	ga	To load a line styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Line Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Load Line Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145588				0	ga	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	ga	To save a line styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Line Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154765				0	ga	To load an arrow styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Load Arrow Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ga	Locate the file containing the arrow styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].soe.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	ga	To save an arrow styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Arrow Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145822				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05200000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Line\"\>Format - Line\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D scenes; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	ga	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	ga	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	ga	Curved object based on Bézier curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	ga	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	ga	3D object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	ga	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	ga	Two types of 3D objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	ga	The Status bar displays "3D scene selected". The 3D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y, and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3D objects. When exporting these 3D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3D bars in charts are of this type, too.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	ga	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2D mode or in a 3D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2D or 3D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	ga	To convert an object to a curved shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	ga	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	ga	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	ga	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	ga	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ga	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	ga	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	ga	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	ga	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	ga	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	ga	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	ga	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	ga	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	ga	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	ga	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318				0	ga	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D Rotation Object\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125				0	ga	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3D Settings toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336				0	ga	You can rotate the 2D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
