helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	ga	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	ga	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	ga	To record a show with rehearse timings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	ga	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150651	6			0	ga	Start the show with the \<emph\>Rehearse Timings\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156396\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rehearsetimings.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156396\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Slide View bar. You see the first slide, and a timer in the bottom corner.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	ga	When it's time to advance to the next slide, click the timer. To keep the default setting for this slide, click the slide, but not the timer. Continue for all slides in your presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	ga	$[officename] has recorded the display time for each slide. Save your presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	ga	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Editing Curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>curves; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting;curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>closing;shapes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>points;adding/converting/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	ga	\<variable id=\"line_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Curves\"\>Editing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	ga	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ga	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	ga	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587				0	ga	To adjust a curved line segment:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	51			0	ga	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ga	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	ga	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	ga	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150431				0	ga	To split a curved line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	ga	You can only split a curved line that has three or more data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392	59			0	ga	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941	60			0	ga	Select a data point, and then click the \<emph\>Split Curve \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150655				0	ga	To create a closed shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150743	62			0	ga	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153080	63			0	ga	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Close Bézier\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145162				0	ga	To convert a data point on a curved line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336	64			0	ga	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	ga	Click the data point you want to convert, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ga	To convert the data point to a smooth point, click the \<emph\>Smooth Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	ga	To convert the data point to a symmetrical point, click the \<emph\>Symmetric Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348				0	ga	To convert the data point to a corner point, click the \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150471				0	ga	To add a data point:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373	69			0	ga	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156256	70			0	ga	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Insert Points\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	ga	Click the line where you want to add the point, and drag a short distance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643				0	ga	If a data point does not have a control point, select the data point, and then click the \<emph\>Convert to Curve\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	ga	To delete a data point:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	74			0	ga	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261				0	ga	Click the point you want to delete.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
