helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Using Gluepoints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	bm_id0919200803534995				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>glue points;using\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ga	\<variable id=\"gluepoints\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/gluepoints.xhp\"\>Using Gluepoints\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803040964				0	ga	In Impress and Draw, you can connect each two shapes with a line called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\"\>connector\</link\>. When you draw a connector between shapes, the connector will be attached to a gluepoint on each shape. Each shape has some default gluepoints, and the positions of the default gluepoints depend on the specific shape. You can add your own custom gluepoints to a shape and then attach connectors to the custom gluepoints.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041099				0	ga	To add and edit gluepoints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id091920080304108				0	ga	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041082				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Drawing toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041186				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Glue Points\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041160				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Gluepoints toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041115				0	ga	Click inside the shape where you want to add the new gluepoint.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041133				0	ga	If the shape is filled, you can click anywhere inside the shape. If the shape is unfilled, you can click the border to insert a glue point. Once inserted, you can drag the glue point to another position inside the shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041250				0	ga	With the four icons next to the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon, you choose the directions which will be permitted for a connector at this gluepoint. You can choose one or more directions for a particular gluepoint.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041298				0	ga	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is active, the gluepoint moves when you resize the object to keep its position relative to the object borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041223				0	ga	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is not active, the icons next to it are no longer grayed out. With these icons you can decide where a gluepoint will be placed when the size of the object is changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Showing a Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	bm_id5592516				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>running slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide transitions;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide transition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	ga	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	ga	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	ga	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	ga	Running a Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	ga	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	ga	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	ga	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	ga	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	ga	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	ga	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	ga	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	ga	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	ga	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	ga	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	ga	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	ga	Running a slide show from a file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	ga	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	ga	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	ga	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
