helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3166462				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Custom Animation\</emph\> dialog, click a tab page to choose from a category of effects. Click an effect, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	ga	To preview the animation, click the \<emph\>Play\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id2476577				0	ga	To apply and edit a motion path effect:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4217047				0	ga	An object can be animated to move along a motion path. You can use predefined or your own motion paths.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id2629474				0	ga	If you select "Curve", "Polygon", or "Freeform Line", the dialog closes and you can draw your own path. If the drawing is finished and not canceled, the created path is removed from the document and inserted as a motion path effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id8069704				0	ga	 \<emph\>Editing motion paths\</emph\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4524674				0	ga	If the Custom Animation Panel is visible, the motion paths of all effects of the current slide are drawn as a transparent overlay on the slide. All paths are visible all the time, therefore animations with consecutive paths can be created easily. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4396801				0	ga	A motion path can be selected by clicking on the path. A selected path will support handles, it can be moved and resized like a shape. A double click on a path starts the point edit mode. The point edit mode can also be started by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Points\</item\> or by pressing \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F8\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148387				0	ga	To remove an animation effect from an object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	ga	On a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the object from which to remove the effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Animation\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3153718				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152596				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>slide designs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; designing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>master pages, see slide masters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ga	\<variable id=\"masterpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/masterpage.xhp\" name=\"Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\"\>Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	ga	Every slide in a presentation has exactly one slide master, also known as master page. A slide master determines the text formatting style for the title and outline and the background design for all slides that use this slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	ga	To apply a new slide master				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	ga	Select \<emph\>Format - Slide Design\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Load\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ga	Under \<emph\>Categories\</emph\>, select a slide design category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915	26			0	ga	Under \<emph\>Templates\</emph\>, select a template with the design that you want to apply. To preview the template, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>, and then select the \<emph\>Preview \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	ga	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	ga	To apply the slide design to all of the slides in your presentation, select the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	ga	To apply the slide design to the current slide only, clear the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
