helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656				0	ga	\<variable id=\"align_arrange\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/align_arrange.xhp\" name=\"Arranging and Aligning Objects\"\>Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ga	Arranging Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727				0	ga	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object, proceed as follows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	ga	Click the object whose position you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	ga	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	ga	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	ga	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	ga	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	ga	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	ga	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	ga	Click the object whose position you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ga	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789				0	ga	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	ga	Shift-click both objects to select them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425				0	ga	Aligning Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	ga	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	ga	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	ga	Distributing Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ga	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	ga	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	ga	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	ga	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Adding Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153144				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>legends; drawings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153144				0	ga	\<variable id=\"text_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/text_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Text\"\>Adding Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	ga	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	ga	Text in a text box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	ga	Text that changes character size to fill the frame size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	ga	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	ga	Text that is copied from a Writer document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	ga	Text that is inserted from a text document or HTML document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	ga	Adding a Text Box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	ga	Drag a text box to the size you want in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	ga	Type or paste your text into the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	ga	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text box to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437				0	ga	Fitting Text to Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	ga	Create a text box as described in the steps above.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	ga	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	ga	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155955				0	ga	Text Tied to a Graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	ga	You can add text to any graphic after double-clicking the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	ga	To determine the position of the text, use the settings in \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147366	59			0	ga	For example, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Callouts\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154508\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_calloutshapes.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154508\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Callouts toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FD				0	ga	Select a callout and move the mouse pointer to where you want the callout to start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150272				0	ga	Drag to draw the callout.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1978514				0	ga	Enter the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091A				0	ga	Copying Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10921				0	ga	Select the text in your Writer document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10925				0	ga	Copy the text to the clipboard (\<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092D				0	ga	Click the page or slide where you want to paste the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10931				0	ga	Paste the text using \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093C				0	ga	Using \<emph\>Paste special\</emph\>, you can choose the text format to be pasted. Depending on formats, you can copy different text attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093F				0	ga	Importing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10946				0	ga	Click the page or slide where you want to import the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1094A				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10952				0	ga	Select a text file (*.txt) or an HTML file and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Insert Text\</emph\> dialog opens. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to insert the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Grouping Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	ga	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	ga	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	ga	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	ga	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ga	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	ga	To group objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	ga	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ga	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002				0	ga	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	ga	Selecting Objects in a Group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	ga	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ga	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Drawing Sectors and Segments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	ga	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	ga	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	ga	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	ga	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	ga	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	ga	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361				0	ga	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	ga	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	ga	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	ga	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581				0	ga	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	ga	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Assembling 3D Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154014				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; assembling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assembled objects in 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combining;3D objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>joining;3D objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	ga	\<variable id=\"join_objects3d\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/join_objects3d.xhp\" name=\"Assembling 3D Objects\"\>Assembling 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	ga	3D objects that each form a 3D scene can be combined into a single 3D scene.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	ga	To combine 3D objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	ga	Insert a 3D object from the \<emph\>3D Objects\</emph\> toolbar (for example, a cube).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	ga	Insert a second slightly larger 3D object (for example, a sphere).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	ga	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	ga	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
