helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	ga	\<variable id=\"cross_fading\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/cross_fading.xhp\" name=\"Cross-Fading Two Objects\"\>Cross-Fading Two Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ga	Cross-fading creates shapes and distributes them by uniform increments between two drawing objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112				0	ga	The cross-fading command is only available in $[officename] Draw. You can, however, copy and paste cross-faded objects into $[officename] Impress.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149209				0	ga	To cross-fade two objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	ga	Hold down Shift and click each object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cross-fading\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	ga	Enter a value to specify the number of objects between the start and end of the cross-fade in the \<emph\>Increments\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3149405				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	ga	A group containing the two original objects and the specified number (increments) of cross-faded objects is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/ueberblenden.png\" width=\"74.88mm\" height=\"65.62mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Illustration for crossfading\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	ga	You can edit the individual objects of a group by selecting the group and pressing F3. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F3 to exit the group editing mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Editing - Cross-fading\"\>Editing - Cross-fading\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
