helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	DATE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155511				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>DATE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155511				0	ga	\<variable id=\"date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_date.xhp\"\>DATE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153551				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATUM\"\>This function calculates a date specified by year, month, day and displays it in the cell's formatting.\</ahelp\> The default format of a cell containing the DATE function is the date format, but you can format the cells with any other number format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148590				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150474				0	ga	DATE(Year; Month; Day)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152815				0	ga	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9957 or between 0 and 99.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153222				0	ga	In \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General \</item\>you can set from which year a two-digit number entry is recognized as 20xx.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155817				0	ga	\<emph\>Month\</emph\> is an integer indicating the month.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	ga	\<emph\>Day\</emph\> is an integer indicating the day of the month.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	ga	If the values for month and day are out of bounds, they are carried over to the next digit. If you enter \<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;12;31)\</item\> the result will be 12/31/00. If, on the other hand, you enter \<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;13;31)\</item\> the result will be 1/31/01.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152589				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;1;31)\</item\> yields 1/31/00 if the cell format setting is MM/DD/YY.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
