helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152793				0	ga	=XIRR(B1:B5; A1:A5; 0.1) returns 0.1828.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149198				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>XNPV function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149198				0	ga	XNPV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153904				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_XNPV\"\>Calculates the capital value (net present value)for a list of payments which take place on different dates.\</ahelp\> The calculation is based on a 365 days per year basis, ignoring leap years.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN11138				0	ga	If the payments take place at regular intervals, use the NPV function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155323				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150117				0	ga	XNPV(Rate; Values; Dates)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153100				0	ga	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the internal rate of return for the payments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155395				0	ga	\<emph\>Values\</emph\> and \<emph\>Dates\</emph\> refer to a series of payments and the series of associated date values. The first pair of dates defines the start of the payment plan. All other date values must be later, but need not be in any order. The series of values must contain at least one negative and one positive value (receipts and deposits)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148832				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150525				0	ga	Calculation of the net present value for the above-mentioned five payments for a notional internal rate of return of 6%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149910				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XNPV(0.06;B1:B5;A1:A5)\</item\> returns 323.02.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148822				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rates of return\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RRI function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148822				0	ga	RRI				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154293				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZGZ\"\>Calculates the interest rate resulting from the profit (return) of an investment.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148444				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148804				0	ga	RRI(P; PV; FV)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154901				0	ga	\<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of periods needed for calculating the interest rate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	ga	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present (current) value. The cash value is the deposit of cash or the current cash value of an allowance in kind. As a deposit value a positive value must be entered; the deposit must not be 0 or <0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149771				0	ga	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> determines what is desired as the cash value of the deposit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148941				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154212				0	ga	For four periods (years) and a cash value of 7,500 currency units, the interest rate of the return is to be calculated if the future value is 10,000 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775	246			0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RRI(4;7500;10000)\</item\> = 7.46 %				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145413	247			0	ga	The interest rate must be 7.46 % so that 7,500 currency units will become 10,000 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154267				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RATE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154267				0	ga	RATE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151052				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZINS\"\>Returns the constant interest rate per period of an annuity.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3158423				0	ga	RATE(NPer; Pmt; PV; FV; Type; Guess)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148910				0	ga	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which payments are made (payment period).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	ga	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the constant payment (annuity) paid during each period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149160				0	ga	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the cash value in the sequence of payments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3166456				0	ga	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the future value, which is reached at the end of the periodic payments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153243				0	ga	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date of the periodic payment, either at the beginning or at the end of a period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	ga	\<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) determines the estimated value of the interest with iterative calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149791				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150706				0	ga	What is the constant interest rate for a payment period of 3 periods if 10 currency units are paid regularly and the present cash value is 900 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RATE(3;10;900)\</item\> = -121% The interest rate is therefore 121%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149106				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>INTRATE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149106				0	ga	INTRATE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_INTRATE\"\>Calculates the annual interest rate that results when a security (or other item) is purchased at an investment value and sold at a redemption value. No interest is paid.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149974				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149800				0	ga	INTRATE(Settlement; Maturity; Investment; Redemption; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	ga	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148988				0	ga	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security is sold.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154604				0	ga	\<emph\>Investment\</emph\> is the purchase price.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154337				0	ga	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the selling price.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145380				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149426				0	ga	A painting is bought on 1990-01-15 for 1 million and sold on 2002-05-05 for 2 million. The basis is daily balance calculation (basis = 3). What is the average annual level of interest?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151125				0	ga	=INTRATE("1990-01-15"; "2002-05-05"; 1000000; 2000000; 3) returns 8.12%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148654				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>COUPNCD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148654				0	ga	COUPNCD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149927				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPNCD\"\>Returns the date of the first interest date after the settlement date. Format the result as a date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153317				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150423				0	ga	COUPNCD(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150628				0	ga	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536				0	ga	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	ga	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155424				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154794				0	ga	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) when is the next interest date?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159251				0	ga	=COUPNCD("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2001-05-15.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143281				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>COUPDAYS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143281				0	ga	COUPDAYS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149488				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPDAYS\"\>Returns the number of days in the current interest period in which the settlement date falls.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148685				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	ga	COUPDAYS(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152767				0	ga	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	ga	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146126				0	ga	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153705				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	ga	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days are there in the interest period in which the settlement date falls?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156338				0	ga	=COUPDAYS("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 181.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154832				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>COUPDAYSNC function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154832				0	ga	COUPDAYSNC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147100				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPDAYSNC\"\>Returns the number of days from the settlement date until the next interest date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151312				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155121				0	ga	COUPDAYSNC(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3158440				0	ga	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146075				0	ga	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154620	159			0	ga	\<emph\>Frequency \</emph\>is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155604				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148671				0	ga	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days are there until the next interest payment?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156158				0	ga	=COUPDAYSNC("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 110.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150408				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>COUPDAYBS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>durations;first interest payment until settlement date\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>securities;first interest payment until settlement date\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150408				0	ga	COUPDAYBS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146795				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPDAYBS\"\>Returns the number of days from the first day of interest payment on a security until the settlement date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156142				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159083				0	ga	COUPDAYBS(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146907				0	ga	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390				0	ga	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154414				0	ga	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153880				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	ga	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days is this?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151103				0	ga	=COUPDAYBS("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 71.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152957				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>COUPPCD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates;interest date prior to settlement date\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152957				0	ga	COUPPCD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPPCD\"\>Returns the date of the interest date prior to the settlement date. Format the result as a date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
