helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150111				0	ga	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> calculates the type of difference. Possible values include 0 (interval) and 1 (in calendar months).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159094				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>ROT13 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>encrypting text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159094				0	ga	ROT13				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_ROT13\"\>Encrypts a character string by moving the characters 13 positions in the alphabet.\</ahelp\> After the letter Z, the alphabet begins again (Rotation). By applying the encryption function again to the resulting code, you can decrypt the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150893				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3159205				0	ga	ROT13(Text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	ga	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is the character string to be encrypted. ROT13(ROT13(Text)) decrypts the code.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151300				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>DAYSINYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of days; in a specific year\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151300				0	ga	DAYSINYEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3143220				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DAYSINYEAR\"\>Calculates the number of days of the year in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145358				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	ga	DAYSINYEAR(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153803				0	ga	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is any date in the respective year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153487				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	ga	=DAYSINYEAR(A1) returns 366 days if A1 contains 1968-02-29, a valid date for the year 1968.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
