helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157993				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCOSHYP\"\>Returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145295				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	ga	ACOSH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149000	64			0	ga	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cosine is Number. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6393932				0	ga	 Number must be greater than or equal to 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150566				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(1)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id951567				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(COSH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149027				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>ACOT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149027				0	ga	ACOT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155818				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOT\"\>Returns the inverse cotangent (the arccotangent) of the given number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153225				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158419				0	ga	ACOT(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948				0	ga	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose cotangent is Number. The angle returned is between 0 and PI.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5834528				0	ga	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147538				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155375				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOT(1)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8589434				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ACOT(1))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
