helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156305				0	ga	ASIN(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	ga	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose sine is Number. The angle returned is between -PI/2 and +PI/2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id203863				0	ga	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149448				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASIN(0)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6853846				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASIN(1)\</item\> returns 1.5707963267949 (PI/2 radians). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8772240				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ASIN(0.5))\</item\> returns 30. The sine of 30 degrees is 0.5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
