helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148803				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_COS\"\>Returns the cosine of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150779				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154213				0	ga	COS(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ga	 Returns the (trigonometric) cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id831019				0	ga	To return the cosine of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153579				0	ga	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147240				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COS(PI()/2)\</item\> returns 0, the cosine of PI/2 radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COS(RADIANS(60))\</item\> returns 0.5, the cosine of 60 degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154277				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>COSH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
