helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145659				0	ga	\<variable id=\"today\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_today.xhp\"\>TODAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3153759				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HEUTE\"\>Returns the current computer system date.\</ahelp\> The value is updated when you reopen the document or modify the values of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154051				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3153154				0	ga	TODAY()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3154741				0	ga	 TODAY is a function without arguments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153627				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>TODAY()\</item\> returns the current computer system date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	DAYS360 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148555				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>DAYS360 function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148555				0	ga	\<variable id=\"days360\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_days360.xhp\"\>DAYS360\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE360\"\>Returns the difference between two dates based on the 360 day year used in interest calculations.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155347				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3155313				0	ga	DAYS360("Date1"; "Date2"; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	ga	If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is earlier than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\>, the function will return a negative number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3151064				0	ga	The optional argument \<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of difference calculation. If Type = 0 or if the argument is missing, the US method (NASD, National Association of Securities Dealers) is used. If Type <> 0, the European method is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148641				0	ga	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348				0	ga	=DAYS360("2000-01-01";NOW()) returns the number of interest days from January 1, 2000 until today.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	DATEVALUE 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145621				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>DATEVALUE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145621				0	ga	\<variable id=\"datevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_datevalue.xhp\"\>DATEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATWERT\"\>Returns the internal date number for text in quotes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	ga	The internal date number is returned as a number. The number is determined by the date system that is used by $[officename] to calculate dates.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903491982				0	ga	If the text string also includes a time value, DATEVALUE only returns the integer part of the conversion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156294				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149268				0	ga	DATEVALUE("Text")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3154819	23			0	ga	         \<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid date expression and must be entered with quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156309				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155841	25			0	ga	         \<emph\>=DATEVALUE("1954-07-20")\</emph\> yields 19925.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
