helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	NETWORKDAYS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151254				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>NETWORKDAYS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151254				0	ga	\<variable id=\"networkdays\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_networkdays.xhp\"\>NETWORKDAYS\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3153788				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_NETWORKDAYS\"\>Returns the number of workdays between a \<emph\>start date and an end date\</emph\>. Holidays can be deducted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148677				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3145775				0	ga	NETWORKDAYS(StartDate; EndDate; Holidays)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3153885				0	ga	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ga	\<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> is the date up until when the calculation is carried out. If the end date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3154115				0	ga	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> is an optional list of holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146902				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3154661				0	ga	How many workdays fall between 2001-12-15 and 2002-01-15? The start date is located in C3 and the end date in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3147328				0	ga	=NETWORKDAYS(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 17 workdays.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Show Details				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153561				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>tables; showing details\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080200.xhp\" name=\"Show Details\"\>Show Details\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowDetail\"\>Shows the details of the grouped row or column that contains the cursor. To show the details of all of the grouped rows or columns, select the outlined table, and then choose this command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922	3			0	ga	To hide a selected group, choose \<emph\>Data -Outline – \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080100.xhp\" name=\"Hide Details\"\>\<emph\>Hide Details\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Lorg Fasaigh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>cells; tracing precedents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula cells;tracing precedents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030100.xhp\" name=\"Trace Precedents\"\>Trace Precedents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowPrecedents\"\>This function shows the relationship between the current cell containing a formula and the cells used in the formula.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	ga	Traces are displayed in the sheet with marking arrows. At the same time, the range of all the cells contained in the formula of the current cell is highlighted with a blue frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	ga	This function is based on a principle of layers. For example, if the precedent cell to a formula is already indicated with a tracer arrow, when you repeat this command, the tracer arrows are drawn to the precedent cells of this cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Protecting document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	ga	Protecting document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	ga	\<variable id=\"dokumenttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToolProtectionDocument\"\>Protects the sheet structure of your document from modifications. It is impossible to insert, delete, rename, move or copy sheets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Open the \<emph\>Protect document\</emph\> dialog with \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\>. Optionally enter a password and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	ga	The structure of protected spreadsheet documents can be changed only if the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> option is disabled. On the context menus for the spreadsheet tabs at the lower graphic border, only the menu item \<emph\>Select All Sheets\</emph\> can be activated. All other menu items are deactivated. To remove the protection, call up the command \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\> again. If no password is assigned, protection is immediately removed. If you were assigned a password, the \<emph\>Remove Spreadsheet Protection\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you must enter the password. Only then can you remove the check mark specifying that protection is active.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	7			0	ga	A protected document, once saved, can only be saved again with the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> menu command. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ga	Password (optional)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	ga	You can create a password to protect your document against unauthorized or accidental modifications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	9			0	ga	You can completely protect your work by combining both options from \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, including password entry. If you want to prevent the document from being opened by other users, select \<emph\>Save With Password \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button. The \<emph\>Enter Password\</emph\> dialog appears. Consider carefully when choosing a password; if you forget it after you close a document you will be unable to access the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Statistical Functions Part One				2002-02-02 02:02:02
