helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154599				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>PERMUT function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>number of permutations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154599				0	ga	PERMUT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154334				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VARIATIONEN\"\>Returns the number of permutations for a given number of objects.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149422				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148466				0	ga	PERMUT(Count1; Count2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148656	148			0	ga	            \<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the total number of objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	149			0	ga	            \<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of objects in each permutation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153351				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150424	151			0	ga	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUT(6;3)\</item\> returns 120. There are 120 different possibilities, to pick a sequence of 3 playing cards out of 6 playing cards.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143276				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>PERMUTATIONA function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143276				0	ga	PERMUTATIONA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3144759				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VARIATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of permutations for a given number of objects (repetition allowed).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145598				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298				0	ga	PERMUTATIONA(Count1; Count2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156139	157			0	ga	            \<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the total number of objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149519	158			0	ga	            \<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of objects in each permutation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151382				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	ga	How often can 2 objects be selected from a total of 11 objects?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	161			0	ga	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(11;2)\</item\> returns 121.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150622	162			0	ga	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PERMUTATIONA(6;3)\</item\> returns 216. There are 216 different possibilities to put a sequence of 3 playing cards together out of six playing cards if every card is returned before the next one is drawn.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152952				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>PROB function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	ga	PROB				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154110				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHRSCHBEREICH\"\>Returns the probability that values in a range are between two limits.\</ahelp\> If there is no \<item type=\"literal\"\>End\</item\> value, this function calculates the probability based on the principle that the Data values are equal to the value of \<item type=\"literal\"\>Start\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146810				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3147330				0	ga	PROB(Data; Probability; Start; End)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	168			0	ga	            \<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	169			0	ga	            \<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the array or range of the corresponding probabilities.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151107	170			0	ga	            \<emph\>Start\</emph\> is the start value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153694	171			0	ga	            \<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the end value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed. If this parameter is missing, the probability for the \<emph\>Start \</emph\>value is calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	173			0	ga	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PROB(A1:A50;B1:B50;50;60)\</item\> returns the probability with which a value within the range of A1:A50 is also within the limits between 50 and 60. Every value within the range of A1:A50 has a probability within the range of B1:B50.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150941				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>WEIBULL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150941				0	ga	WEIBULL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WEIBULL\"\>Returns the values of the Weibull distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372767				0	ga	The Weibull distribution is a continuous probability distribution, with parameters Alpha > 0 (shape) and Beta > 0 (scale). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372777				0	ga	If C is 0, WEIBULL calculates the probability density function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372743				0	ga	If C is 1, WEIBULL calculates the cumulative distribution function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159393				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478				0	ga	WEIBULL(Number; Alpha; Beta; C)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151317	179			0	ga	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value at which to calculate the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3158436	180			0	ga	            \<emph\>Alpha \</emph\>is the shape parameter of the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668	181			0	ga	            \<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the scale parameter of the Weibull distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	182			0	ga	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> indicates the type of function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146077	184			0	ga	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=WEIBULL(2;1;1;1)\</item\> returns 0.86.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372899				0	ga	See also the \<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Calc:_WEIBULL_function\"\>Wiki page\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
