helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10904				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Choose the field that you want to view the details for.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140200.xhp\" name=\"Right\"\>Right\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillRight\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two columns with the contents of the left most cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	ga	If a range of only one row is selected, the contents of the far left cell are copied to all the other selected cells. If you have selected several rows, each of the far left cells is copied into those cells to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Statistical Functions Part Four				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	ga	\<variable id=\"mq\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060184.xhp\" name=\"Statistical Functions Part Four\"\>Statistical Functions Part Four\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154511				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>MAX function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	ga	MAX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAX\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id9282509				0	ga	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	ga	MAX(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	6			0	ga	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166426				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>MAXA function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166426				0	ga	MAXA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAXA\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments. In opposite to MAX, here you can enter text. The value of the text is 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id7689443				0	ga	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150516				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3166431				0	ga	MAXA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	ga	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156290				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156446				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200;"Text")\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>MEDIAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	ga	MEDIAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MEDIAN\"\>Returns the median of a set of numbers. In a set containing an uneven number of values, the median will be the number in the middle of the set and in a set containing an even number of values, it will be the mean of the two values in the middle of the set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148871				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	ga	MEDIAN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	ga	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are values or ranges, which represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144506				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	ga	for an odd number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20;21)\</item\> returns 9 as the median value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ga	for an even number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20)\</item\> returns the average of the two middle values 5 and 9, thus 7.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154541				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>MIN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154541				0	ga	MIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MIN\"\>Returns the minimum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id2301400				0	ga	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154651				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146964				0	ga	MIN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153486				0	ga	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155523				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154734				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MIN(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the smallest value in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147504				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>MINA function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147504				0	ga	MINA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147249				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MINA\"\>Returns the minimum value in a list of arguments. Here you can also enter text. The value of the text is 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id4294564				0	ga	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150435				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153336				0	ga	MINA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146098				0	ga	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148743				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147401				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINA(1;"Text";20)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the smallest value in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166465				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>AVEDEV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages;statistical functions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
