helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ViewValueHighlighting\"\>Displays cell contents in different colors, depending on type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	ga	To remove the highlighting, unmark the menu entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	ga	Text cells are formatted in black, formulas in green, and number cells in blue, no matter how their display is formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	ga	If this function is active, colors that you define in the document will not be displayed. When you deactivate the function, the user-defined colors are displayed again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
