helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3156132				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=GESTEP(5;1)\</item\> returns 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147276				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>HEX2BIN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;hexadecimal numbers, into binary numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147276				0	ga	HEX2BIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3150258				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_HEX2BIN\"\>The result is the binary number for the hexadecimal number entered.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156117				0	ga	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3155847				0	ga	HEX2BIN(Number; Places)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	ga	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is a hexadecimal number. The number can have a maximum of 10 places. The most significant bit is the sign bit, the following bits return the value. Negative numbers are entered as two's complement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3153758				0	ga	\<emph\>Places\</emph\> is the number of places to be output.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154052				0	ga	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3156002				0	ga	\<item type=\"input\"\>=HEX2BIN(64;8)\</item\> returns 01100100.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
