helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156178				0	ga	FORMAT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150220				0	ga	Returns a character string that indicates the number format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	ga	, = number with thousands separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153837				0	ga	F = number without thousands separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150318				0	ga	C = currency format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153168				0	ga	S = exponential representation, for example, 1.234+E56				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153515				0	ga	P = percentage				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154375				0	ga	In the above formats, the number of decimal places after the decimal separator is given as a number. Example: the number format #,##0.0 returns ,1 and the number format 00.000% returns P3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
