helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5383465				0	ga	You cannot apply borders to multiple selections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7790154				0	ga	Default Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2918485				0	ga	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	ga	The thin gray lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5212561				0	ga	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4818872				0	ga	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id8989226				0	ga	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id622577				0	ga	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8119754				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id7261268\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.0937in\" height=\"0.2189in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7261268\"\>default icon row of Borders tab page\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8964201				0	ga	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders, all inner lines, and all diagonal lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6048463				0	ga	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1495406				0	ga	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed, except the diagonal lines, which will be removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9269386				0	ga	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3593554				0	ga	User Defined Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4018066				0	ga	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8004699				0	ga	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8037659				0	ga	Line types				2002-02-02 02:02:02
