helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Renaming Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>renaming;sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	ga	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	ga	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	ga	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	ga	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502833				0	ga	Sheet names can contain almost any character. Some naming restrictions apply when you want to save the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050283				0	ga	When saving to Microsoft Excel format, the following characters are not allowed in sheet names:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050281				0	ga	colon :				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502897				0	ga	back slash \\				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050299				0	ga	forward slash /				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502913				0	ga	question mark ?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050298				0	ga	asterisk *				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502969				0	ga	left square bracket [				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502910				0	ga	right square bracket ]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502971				0	ga	single quote ' as the first or last character of the name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050307				0	ga	In cell references, a sheet name has to be enclosed in single quotes ' if the name contains other characters than alphanumeric or underscore. A single quote contained within a name has to be escaped by doubling it (two single quotes). For example, you want to reference the cell A1 on a sheet with the following name:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503071				0	ga	This year's sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503054				0	ga	The reference must be enclosed in single quotes, and the one single quote inside the name must be doubled:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503069				0	ga	'This year''s sheet'.A1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444				0	ga	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Entering Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>values; inserting in multiple cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;selecting for data entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>areas, see also cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3405255				0	ga	\<variable id=\"cell_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_enter.xhp\"\>Entering Values\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7147129				0	ga	Calc can simplify entering data and values into multiple cells. You can change some settings to conform to your preferences.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id5621509				0	ga	To Enter Values Into a Range of Cells Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8200018				0	ga	There are two features that assist you when you enter a block of data manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id1867427				0	ga	Area Detection for New Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7908871				0	ga	In the row below a heading row, you can advance from one cell to the next with the Tab key. After you enter the value into the last cell in the current row, press Enter. Calc positions the cursor below the first cell of the current block.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6196783				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id6473586\" src=\"res/helpimg/area1.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6473586\"\>area detection\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8118839				0	ga	In row 3, press Tab to advance from cell B3 to C3, D3, and E3. Then press Enter to advance to B4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3583788				0	ga	Area Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id2011780				0	ga	Use drag-and-drop to select the area where you want to input values. But start dragging from the last cell of the area and release the mouse button when you have selected the first cell. Now you can start to input values. Always press the Tab key to advance to the next cell. You will not leave the selected area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7044282				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id2811365\" src=\"res/helpimg/area2.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2811365\"\>area selection\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3232520				0	ga	Select the area from E7 to B3. Now B3 is waiting for your input. Press Tab to advance to the next cell within the selected area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id8950163				0	ga	To Enter Values to a Range of Cells Automatically				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id633869				0	ga	See \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Rotating Tables (Transposing)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
