helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	ga	\<variable id=\"table_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Tables (Transposing)\"\>Rotating Tables (Transposing)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	ga	In $[officename] Calc, there is a way to "rotate" a spreadsheet so that rows become columns and columns become rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	ga	Select the cell range that you want to transpose.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	ga	Click the cell that is to be the top left cell in the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	ga	In the dialog, mark \<emph\>Paste all\</emph\> and \<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	ga	If you now click OK the columns and rows are transposed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Paste Special\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBASE\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dBASE import/export\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing from/exporting to dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;importing dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	ga	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	ga	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	ga	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	ga	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	ga	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	ga	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	ga	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	ga	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
