helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	ga	\<variable id=\"text_wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_wrap.xhp\" name=\"Writing Multi-line Text\"\>Writing Multi-line Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ga	Pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys inserts a manual line break. This shortcut only works directly in the cell, not in the input line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	ga	If you want the text to automatically break at the right border of the cell, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	ga	Select all the cells where you want the text to break at the right border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	ga	In \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\> option and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell\"\>Format - Cell\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	ga	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	ga	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ga	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ga	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	ga	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	ga	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	ga	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in other sheets/documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents;references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	ga	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	ga	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	ga	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	ga	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	ga	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	ga	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	ga	               \<item type=\"literal\"\>=Sheet2.A1\</item\>            				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	ga	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	ga	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	ga	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	ga	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	ga	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	ga	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	ga	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	ga	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	ga	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Recognizing Names as Addressing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148797				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>automatic addressing in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>natural language addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; using row/column labels\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; as addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>name recognition on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>row headers;using in formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>column headers;using in formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognizing; column and row labels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	ga	\<variable id=\"address_auto\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/address_auto.xhp\" name=\"Recognizing Names as Addressing\"\>Recognizing Names as Addressing\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	ga	You can use cells with text to refer to the rows or to the columns that contain the cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3154942\" src=\"res/helpimg/names_as_addressing.png\" width=\"2.1291in\" height=\"0.8709in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154942\"\>Example spreadsheet\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512				0	ga	In the example spreadsheet, you can use the string \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column One'\</item\> in a formula to refer to the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>B5\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>C2\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>C5\</item\>. You can also use \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row One'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D3\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B4\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D4\</item\>. The result of a formula that uses a cell name, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>SUM('Column One')\</item\>, is 600.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	ga	This function is active by default. To turn this function off, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Automatically find column and row labels\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	ga	If you want a name to be automatically recognized by Calc, the name must start with a letter and be composed of alphanumeric characters. If you enter the name in the formula yourself, enclose the name in single quotation marks ('). If a single quotation mark appears in a name, you must enter a backslash in front of the quotation mark, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Harry\\'s Bar'.\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	ga	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\"\>Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id9520249				0	ga	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for cell ranges in $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144760				0	ga	Applying a Background Color to a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	ga	Select the cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> (or \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> from the context menu).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3152938				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	ga	Graphics in the Background of Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ga	Select the graphic and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153575				0	ga	The graphic is inserted anchored to the current cell. You can move and scale the graphic as you want. In your context menu you can use the \<emph\>Arrange - To Background\</emph\> command to place this in the background. To select a graphic that has been placed in the background, use the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Navigator\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id51576				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>\<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7601245				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Changing Row Height or Column Width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145748				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>heights of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; heights and widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>widths of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;row heights/column widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	ga	\<variable id=\"row_height\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/row_height.xhp\" name=\"Changing Row Height or Column Width\"\>Changing Row Height or Column Width\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	ga	You can change the height of the rows with the mouse or through the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	ga	What is described here for rows and row height applies accordingly for columns and column width.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	ga	Using the mouse to change the row height or column width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	ga	Click the area of the headers on the separator below the current row, keep the mouse button pressed and drag up or down in order to change the row height.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3159237				0	ga	Select the optimal row height by double-clicking the separator below the row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	ga	Using the dialog to change the row height or column width				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150367				0	ga	Click the row so that you achieve the focus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3166432				0	ga	Start the context menu on the header at the left-hand side.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340100.xhp\" name=\"Row height\"\>Row height\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal row height\"\>Optimal row height\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340200.xhp\" name=\"Column width\"\>Column width\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
