helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Deactivating Automatic Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	ga	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	ga	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	ga	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	ga	Automatic Text or Number Completion				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	ga	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	ga	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	ga	Automatic Conversion to Date Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ga	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	ga	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	ga	Quotation Marks Replaced by Custom Quotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	ga	Cell Content Always Begins With Uppercase				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab. Unmark \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	ga	Replace Word With Another Word				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Delete\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Applying Filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>filters; applying/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;removing/redisplaying with filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ga	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ga	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	ga	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect the conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	ga	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id9384746				0	ga	To remove a filter, so that you see all cells again, click inside the area where the filter was applied, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	ga	When you select multiple rows from an area where a filter was applied, then this selection can include rows that are visible and rows that are hidden by the filter. If you then apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the visible rows. The hidden rows are not affected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id218817				0	ga	This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145120				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Calc shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;%PRODUCTNAME Calc accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145120				0	ga	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)\"\>Shortcut Keys (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	ga	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	ga	Cell Selection Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	ga	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"formula/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	ga	In a text box that has a button to minimize the dialog, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	ga	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	ga	Controlling the Outline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	ga	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	ga	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	ga	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	ga	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+1 to Command+8\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	ga	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	ga	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	ga	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343				0	ga	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	ga	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	ga	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	ga	If the selection tool is active, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240				0	ga	With \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 you set the focus to the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	ga	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Validity of Cell Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156442				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>values; limiting on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>limits; specifying value limits on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>permitted cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error messages; defining for incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>actions in case of incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips; defining text for cell input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments;help text for cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining input help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>macros; running when incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; validity check\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	ga	\<variable id=\"validity\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/validity.xhp\" name=\"Validity of Cell Contents\"\>Validity of Cell Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	ga	For each cell, you can define entries to be valid. Invalid entries to a cell will be rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ga	The validity rule is activated when a new value is entered. If an invalid value has already been inserted into the cell, or if you insert a value in the cell either with drag-and-drop or by copying and pasting, the validity rule will not take effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id5174718				0	ga	You can choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective\</emph\> at any time and choose the command \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>\<emph\>Mark Invalid Data\</emph\>\</link\> to display which cells contain invalid values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	ga	Using Cell Contents Validity				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	ga	Select the cells for which you want to define a new validity rule.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	8			0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validity\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156020	9			0	ga	On the \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> tab page, enter the conditions for new values entered into cells. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159208				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Allow\</emph\> field, select an option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	ga	If you select "Whole Numbers", values such as "12.5" are not allowed. Choosing "Date" allows date information both in the local date format as well as in the form of a \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"serial date\"\>serial date\</link\>. Similarly, the "Time" condition permits time values such as "12:00" or serial time numbers. "Text Length" stipulates that cells are allowed to contain text only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id9224829				0	ga	Select "List" to enter a list of valid entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149317				0	ga	Select the next condition under \<emph\>Data\</emph\>. According to what you choose, additional options will be selectable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	ga	After you have determined the conditions for cell validity, you can use the other two tab pages to create message boxes:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159261				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Input Help\</emph\> tab page, enter the title and the text of the tip, which will then be displayed if the cell is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page, select the action to be carried out in the event of an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416				0	ga	If you select "Stop" as the action, invalid entries are not accepted, and the previous cell contents are retained.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	ga	Select "Warning" or "Information" to display a dialog in which the entry can either be canceled or accepted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	ga	If you select "Macro", then by using the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button you can specify a macro to be run in the event of an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149011	35			0	ga	To display the error message, select \<emph\>Show error message when invalid values are entered\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	ga	After changing the action for a cell on the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page and closing the dialog with OK, you must first select another cell before the change takes effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3154805				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Validity\"\>Data - Validity\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Using Print Ranges on a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	bm_id14648				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF export of print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>clearing, see also deleting/removing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extending print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D7				0	ga	\<variable id=\"printranges\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F5				0	ga	You can define which range of cells on a spreadsheet to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FB				0	ga	The cells on the sheet that are not part of the defined print range are not printed or exported. Sheets without a defined print range are not printed and not exported to a PDF file, unless the document uses the Excel file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	ga	For files opened in Excel format, all sheets that do not contain a defined print range are printed. The same behavior occurs when you export the Excel formatted spreadsheet to a PDF file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	ga	To Define a Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	ga	Select the cells that you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10909				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10910				0	ga	To Add Cells to a Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	ga	Select the cells that you want to add to the existing print range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091B				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	ga	To Clear a Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10929				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	ga	Using the Page Break Preview to Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centered page number in gray. Nonprinting areas have a gray background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	ga	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	ga	To View and Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10937				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	ga	To change the default zoom factor of the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, double click the percentage value on the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> bar, and select a new zoom factor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10836				0	ga	Edit the print range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10944				0	ga	To change the size of a print range, drag a border of the range to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	ga	To delete a manual page break that is contained in a print range, drag the border of the page break outside of the print range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10948				0	ga	To clear a print range, drag a border of the range onto the opposite border of the range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	ga	To exit the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CF				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\"\>Editing Print Ranges\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Using Rounded Off Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; rounded off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounded off numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exact numbers in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;number of decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;rounded in calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rounded off values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>precision as shown\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding precision\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; values as shown\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	ga	\<variable id=\"rounding_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rounding_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Using Rounded Off Numbers\"\>Using Rounded Off Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ga	In $[officename] Calc, all decimal numbers are displayed rounded off to two decimal places.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ga	To change this for selected cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	ga	Mark all the cells you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and go to the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, select \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. Under \<emph\>Options\</emph\>, change the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	ga	To change this everywhere				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ga	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Modify the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154755				0	ga	To calculate with the rounded off numbers instead of the internal exact values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	ga	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Mark the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> field and exit the dialog with OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	ga	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	ga	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	ga	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ga	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	ga	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	ga	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	ga	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" seconds and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	ga	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	ga	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	ga	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Highlighting Negative Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats;colors for negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	ga	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	ga	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	ga	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	ga	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	ga	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format code\</item\>. For example, instead of RED, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>YELLOW\</item\>. If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\> icon, this is a valid entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Copying to Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	ga	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	ga	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	ga	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	ga	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	ga	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154686				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; referencing cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; referencing by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;inserting by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;references, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154686				0	ga	\<variable id=\"cellreference_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreference_dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\"\>Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	ga	With the help of the Navigator you can reference cells from one sheet to another sheet in the same document or in a different document. The cells can be inserted as a copy, link, or hyperlink. The range to be inserted must be defined with a name in the original file so that it can be inserted in the target file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	ga	Open the document that contains the source cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ga	To set the source range as the range, select the cells and choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. Save the source document, and do not close it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	ga	Open the sheet in which you want to insert something.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154732				0	ga	Open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>. In the lower box of the Navigator select the source file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	ga	In the Navigator, the source file object appears under "Range names".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ga	Using the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon in Navigator, choose whether you want the reference to be a hyperlink, link, or copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	ga	Click the name under "Range names" in the Navigator, and drag into the cell of the current sheet where you want to insert the reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	ga	This method can also be used to insert a range from another sheet of the same document into the current sheet. Select the active document as source in step 4 above.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Importing and Exporting Text Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulas as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulas\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	ga	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	ga	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	ga	To Import a CSV File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	ga	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	ga	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	ga	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	ga	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	ga	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	ga	If you want to export the formulas as formulas, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	ga	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	ga	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	ga	In the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	ga	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	ga	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	ga	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	ga	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	ga	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
