helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	ga	Writes a record to a relative file or a sequence of bytes to a binary file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	ga	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020201.xhp\" name=\"Get\"\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>Get\</item\>\</link\> statement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ga	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	ga	Put [#] FileNumber As Integer, [position], Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153190				0	ga	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	ga	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression that defines the file that you want to write to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	8			0	ga	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>For relative files (random access files), the number of the record that you want to write.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	ga	For binary files (binary access), the position of the byte in the file where you want to start writing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729				0	ga	\<emph\>Variable:\</emph\> Name of the variable that you want to write to the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ga	Note for relative files: If the contents of this variable does not match the length of the record that is specified in the \<emph\>Len\</emph\> clause of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> statement, the space between the end of the newly written record and the next record is padded with existing data from the file that you are writing to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	ga	Note for binary files: The contents of the variables are written to the specified position, and the file pointer is inserted directly after the last byte. No space is left between the records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
