helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	ga	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to calculate the natural logarithm for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ga	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. Base e is a constant with an approximate value of 2.718282...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	ga	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	ga	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131				0	ga	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152463				0	ga	Sub ExampleLogExp				2002-02-02 02:02:02
