helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id1006200801025030				0	ga	Marcanna eatraimh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	ga	Príomh:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150397				0	ga	Specifies whether the marks are to be on the inner or outer side of the axis. It is possible to combine both: you will then see marks on both sides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	ga	Inner				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156399				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_TICKS_INNER\"\>Specifies that marks are placed on the inner side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166469				0	ga	Outer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153120				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_TICKS_OUTER\"\>Specifies that marks are placed on the outer side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159128				0	ga	Mion:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146885				0	ga	This area is used to define the marking dashes between the axis marks. It is possible to activate both fields. This will result in a marking line running from the outside to the inside.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150654				0	ga	Inner				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_HELPTICKS_INNER\"\>Specifies that minor interval marks are placed on the inner side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154677				0	ga	Outer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150745				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_HELPTICKS_OUTER\"\>Specifies that minor interval marks are placed on the outer side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id1006200801025271				0	ga	Place marks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id1006200801025278				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select where to place the marks: at labels, at axis, or at axis and labels.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Roghanna				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149400				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>aligning; 2D charts\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>charts; aligning\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>pie charts;options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067				0	ga	Use this dialog to define some options that are available for specific chart types. The contents of the Options dialog vary with the chart type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	ga	Align data series to:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145228				0	ga	In this area you can choose between two Y axis scaling modes. The axes can only be scaled and given properties separately.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	ga	Y-ais phríomhúil				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_1\"\>This option is active as default. All data series are aligned to the primary Y axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143221				0	ga	Y-ais thánaisteach				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_2\"\>Changes the scaling of the Y axis. This axis is only visible when at least one data series is assigned to it and the axis view is active.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166423				0	ga	Socruithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	ga	Define the settings for a bar chart in this area. Any changes apply to all data series of the chart, not to the selected data only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145584				0	ga	Spásáil				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_GAP\"\>Defines the spacing between the columns in percent.\</ahelp\> The maximal spacing is 600%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384				0	ga	Overlap				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156447				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_OVERLAP\"\>Defines the necessary settings for overlapping data series.\</ahelp\> You can choose between -100 and +100%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	ga	Connection Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTIONS:CB_CONNECTOR\"\>For "stacked" and "percent" column (vertical bar) charts, mark this check box to connect the column layers that belong together with lines.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id9842219				0	ga	Show bars side by side				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id9800103				0	ga	If two axes are shown in a bar chart, and some data series are attached to the first axis, while some other data series are attached to the second axis, then both sets of data series are shown independently, overlapping each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2144535				0	ga	As a result, bars attached to the first y-axis are partly or completely hidden by bars attached to the second y-axis. To avoid this, enable the option to display bars side by side. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The bars from different data series are shown as if they were attached only to one axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id24414				0	ga	Clockwise direction				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2527237				0	ga	Available for pie and donut charts. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The default direction in which the pieces of a pie chart are ordered is counterclockwise. Enable the \<emph\>Clockwise direction\</emph\> checkbox to draw the pieces in opposite direction.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id401013				0	ga	Uillinn tosaithe				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id761131				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Drag the small dot along the circle or click any position on the circle to set the starting angle of a pie or donut chart. The starting angle is the mathematical angle position where the first piece is drawn. The value of 90 degrees draws the first piece at the 12 o'clock position. A value of 0 degrees starts at the 3 o'clock position.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id553910				0	ga	In 3D pie and donut charts that were created with older versions of the software, the starting angle is 0 degrees instead of 90 degrees. For old and new 2D charts the default starting angle is 90 degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id1414838				0	ga	When you change the starting angle or the direction, only current versions of the software show the changed values. Older versions of the software display the same document using the default values: Always counterclockwise direction and a starting value of 90 degrees (2D pie charts) or 0 degrees (3D pie charts).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3179723				0	ga	Degrees				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2164067				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the starting angle between 0 and 359 degrees. You can also click the arrows to change the displayed value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524613				0	ga	Breac luachanna ar iarraidh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524650				0	ga	Sometimes values are missing in a data series that is shown in a chart. You can select from different options how to plot the missing values. The options are available for some chart types only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524823				0	ga	Leave gap				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524811				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, no data will be shown. This is the default for chart types Column, Bar, Line, Net.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524811				0	ga	Assume zero				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052489				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the y-value will be shown as zero. This is the default for chart type Area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524837				0	ga	Continue line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524938				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the interpolation from the neighbor values will be shown. This is the default for chart type XY.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524937				0	ga	Include values from hidden cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052494				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check to also show values of currently hidden cells within the source cell range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Chart Type Column and Line 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id5976744				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>column and line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combination charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8596453				0	ga	\<variable id=\"type_column_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Line\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id4818567				0	ga	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id2451551				0	ga	Colún agus Líne				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3101901				0	ga	A Column and Line chart is a combination of a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Column chart\</link\> with a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Line chart\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7910397				0	ga	Select one of the variants				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5244300				0	ga	Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn side by side so that you can easily compare their values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7163609				0	ga	Stacked Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn stacked above each other, so that the height of a column visualizes the sum of the data values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1842097				0	ga	You can insert a second y-axis with \<link href=\"text/schart/01/04040000.xhp\"\>Insert - Axes\</link\> after you finish the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8297677				0	ga	To specify a data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8871120				0	ga	The leftmost columns (or the top rows) of the selected data range provide the data that are shown as Columns objects. The other columns or rows of the data range provide the data for the Lines objects. You can change this assignment in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2952055				0	ga	Select the data range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id594500				0	ga	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1944944				0	ga	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id6667683				0	ga	Organizing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7616809				0	ga	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9770195				0	ga	The column data series are positioned at the top of the list, the line data series at the bottom of the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1446272				0	ga	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3779717				0	ga	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5056611				0	ga	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7786492				0	ga	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This way you can convert a Column data series to a List data series and back. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id265816				0	ga	Editing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6768700				0	ga	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1924497				0	ga	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5081942				0	ga	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2958464				0	ga	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id883816				0	ga	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	ga	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id974456				0	ga	Editing categories or data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2767113				0	ga	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id301828				0	ga	The values in the Categories range will be shown as labels on the x axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8996246				0	ga	Inserting chart elements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5729544				0	ga	Use the Chart Elements page of the Chart Wizard to insert any of the following elements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2932828				0	ga	Chart titles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
