helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152896				0	ga	Y axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary Y axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762	41			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>The major axis and the secondary axis can have different scaling. For example, you can scale one axis to 2 in. and the other to 1.5 in. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Chart Type Stock				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	bm_id2959990				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>stock charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chart types;stock\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data sources;setting for stock charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id966216				0	ga	\<variable id=\"type_stock\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_stock.xhp\"\>Chart Type Stock\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3516953				0	ga	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5268410				0	ga	Stoc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id61342				0	ga	A Stock chart illustrates the market trend given by opening price, bottom price, top price and closing price. The transaction volume can also be shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2131412				0	ga	For a Stock chart the order of the data series is important. The data should be arranged as shown in the example table below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
