helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Barraí Earráide Y				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	ga	\<variable id=\"statistik\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use the \<emph\>Y Error Bars\</emph\> dialog to display error bars for 2D charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3401287				0	ga	An error bar is an indicator line that spans over a range from y - NegativeErrorValue to y + PositiveErrorValue. In this term, y is the value of the data point. When "standard deviation" is selected, y is the mean value of the data series. NegativeErrorValue and PositiveErrorValue are the amounts calculated by the error bar function or given explicitly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	ga	The \<emph\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</emph\> menu command is only available for 2D charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	ga	Error category				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	ga	In the \<emph\>Error category\</emph\> area, you can choose different ways to display the error category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152989				0	ga	Neamhní				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_STAT:RBT_NONE\"\>Does not show any error bars.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145117				0	ga	Constant value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_MINUS\"\>Displays constant values that you specify in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159204				0	ga	Percentage				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150048				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_PERCENT\"\>Displays a percentage. The display refers to the corresponding data point. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id8977629				0	ga	Feidhmeanna				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id7109286				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select a function to calculate the error bars.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5154576				0	ga	Standard Error: Displays the standard error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Variance: Displays the variance calculated from the number of data points and respective values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Standard Deviation: Displays the standard deviation (square root of the variance).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Error Margin: Displays the highest error margin in percent according to the highest value of the data group. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id350962				0	ga	Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6679586				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click Cell Range and then specify a cell range from which to take the positive and negative error bar values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3872188				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click a button to shrink the dialog, then use the mouse to select the cell range in the spreadsheet. Click the button again to restore the dialog to full size.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id2633747				0	ga	Ó Thábla Sonraí				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6633503				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a chart with its own data, the error bar values can be entered in the chart data table. The Data Table dialog shows additional columns titled Positive Y-Error-Bars and Negative Y-Error-Bars.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573839				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to add to the displayed value as the positive error value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573862				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to subtract from the displayed value as the negative error value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573844				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the positive error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573970				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the negative error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0428200810573977				0	ga	Luach céanna sa dá chás				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573991				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable to use the positive error values also as negative error values. You can only change the value of the "Positve (+)" box. That value gets copied to the "Negative (-)" box automatically.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
