helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	ga	\<variable id=\"titel\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertMenuTitles\"\>Opens a dialog to enter or modify the titles in a chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can define the text for the main title, subtitle and the axis labels, and specify if they are displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	ga	Príomhtheideal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150371				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_MAINTITLE\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Main Title\</emph\> option activates the main title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146980				0	ga	Fotheideal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_SUBTITLE\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Subtitle\</emph\> option activates the subtitle. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	ga	\<variable id=\"sytexttitel\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleTitle\"\>Click \<emph\>Title On/Off\</emph\> on the Formatting bar to show or hide the title and subtitle.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156018				0	ga	X axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_X_AXIS\"\>Marking the \<emph\>X axis\</emph\> option activates the X axis title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159226				0	ga	Y axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_Y_AXIS\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Y axis\</emph\> option activates the Y axis title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153009				0	ga	Z axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154710				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_Z_AXIS\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Z axis\</emph\> option activates the Z axis title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\> This option is only available for 3-D charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	ga	\<variable id=\"sytextachse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisTitle\"\>Click \<emph\>Axes Title On/Off\</emph\> on the Formatting bar to show or hide the axis labels.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	3D View 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>3D charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>charts; 3D views\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>illumination; 3D charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3464461				0	ga	\<variable id=\"three_d_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	ga	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> or in the context menu of a chart you can choose a chart type. \<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to edit the properties of a three dimensional view for Column, Bar, Pie, and Area charts. For Line and XY (Scatter) charts you can see 3D lines.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	ga	The chart preview responds to the new settings that you enter in the dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	ga	When you leave the dialog with OK, the settings are applied permanently. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	ga	When you leave the dialog with Cancel or Escape, the chart returns to the state when you opened the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8081911				0	ga	For a 3D chart you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - 3D View\</item\> to set perspective, appearance and illumination.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id2924283				0	ga	Peirspictíocht				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	ga	Enter the values for rotation of the chart on the three axes and for a perspective view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9999694				0	ga	Set all angles to 0 for a front view of the chart. Pie charts and donut charts are shown as circles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2861720				0	ga	With Right-angled axes enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ga	An x value of 90, with y and z set to 0, provides a view from top down to the chart. With x set to -90, you see the bottom of the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ga	The rotations are applied in the order first x, then y, last z.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ga	When shading is enabled and you rotate a chart, the lights are rotated as if they are fixed to the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2578203				0	ga	The rotation axes always relate to the page, not to the chart's axes. This is different from some other chart programs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4923245				0	ga	Select the Perspective check box to view the chart in central perspective as through a camera lens instead of using a parallel projection. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3416547				0	ga	Set the focus length with the spin button. 100% gives a perspective view where a far edge in the chart looks approximately half as big as a near edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	ga	Older versions of %PRODUCTNAME cannot display the percentage of perspective the same way as the current version.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7623828				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Right-angled axes is enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders. Right-angled axes is enabled by default for newly created 3D charts. Pie and Donut charts do not support right-angled axes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the x axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the y axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8915372				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the z axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6070436				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Mark the Perspective box to view the chart as through a camera lens. Use the spin button to set the percentage. With a high percentage nearer objects look bigger than more distant objects.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id7564012				0	ga	Cuma				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	ga	Select a scheme from the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	ga	By selecting a scheme, the check boxes and the light sources are set accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	ga	If you mark or unmark a combination of check boxes that is not given by the Realistic or Simple scheme, you create a Custom scheme.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1579027				0	ga	Mark \<emph\>Shading\</emph\> to use the Gouraud method for rendering the surface, otherwise a flat method is used. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5624561				0	ga	The flat method sets a single color and brightness for each polygon. The edges are visible, soft gradients and spot lights are not possible. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5901058				0	ga	The Gouraud method applies gradients for a smoother, more realistic look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8469191				0	ga	Mark \<emph\>Object Borders\</emph\> to draw lines along the edges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4407483				0	ga	Mark \<emph\>Rounded Edges\</emph\> to smooth the edges of box shapes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a scheme from the list box, or click any of the check boxes below.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies Gouraud shading if marked, or flat shading if unmarked.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows borders around the areas by setting the line style to Solid.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edges are rounded by 5%.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id1939451				0	ga	Soilsiú				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	ga	Set the light sources for the 3D view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6531266				0	ga	Click any of the eight buttons to switch a directed light source on or off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	ga	By default, the second light source is switched on. It is the first of seven "normal", uniform light sources. The light source number one projects a specular light with highlights.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	ga	For the selected light source, you can then choose a color and intensity in the list box just below the eight buttons. The brightness values of all lights are added, so use dark colors when you enable multiple lights.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	ga	The small preview inside this tab page has two sliders to set the vertical and horizontal position of the selected light source. The light source always aims to the middle of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ga	The button in the corner of the small preview switches the internal illumination model between a sphere and a cube.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	ga	Use the Ambient light list box to define the ambient light which shines with a uniform intensity from all directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the right slider to set the vertical height and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the bottom slider to set the horizontal position and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to switch between an illumination model of a sphere or a cube.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the specular light source with highlights.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the uniform light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color using the color dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the ambient light.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5871761				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color using the color dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Chart Type Area				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	bm_id4130680				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>area charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;area\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id310678				0	ga	\<variable id=\"type_area\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_area.xhp\"\>Chart Type Area\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id916776				0	ga	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id961943				0	ga	Méid				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	ga	An area chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series are connected by a line. The area between each two lines is filled with a color. The area chart's focus is to emphasize the changes from one category to the next.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	ga	Normal - this subtype plots all values as absolute y values. It first plots the area of the last column in the data range, then the next to last, and so on, and finally the first column of data is drawn. Thus, if the values in the first column are higher than other values, the last drawn area will hide the other areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id3640247				0	ga	Stacked - this subtypes plots values cumulatively stacked on each other. It ensures that all values are visible, and no data set is hidden by others. However, the y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the last column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id4585100				0	ga	Percent - this subtype plots values cumulatively stacked on each other and scaled as percentage of the category total.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Pointe Sonraí				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Data Point\"\>Data Point\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	ga	This dialog allows you to change the properties of a selected data point. The dialog appears when there is only one data point selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149121				0	ga	Any changes made only affect this one data point. For example, if you edit the color of a bar, only the color of that bar will be different.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Y Axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>Y axes; formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	ga	Y Axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628	2			0	ga	\<variable id=\"yachse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramAxisY\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Y Axis \</emph\>dialog, to change properties of the Y axis.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Character\"\>Character\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Grid				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>X axes;grid formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Y axes;grid formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Z axes; grid formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	ga	Grid				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	ga	\<variable id=\"gitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramGridAll\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Grid\</emph\> dialog for defining grid properties.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Chart Type Column and Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	bm_id4919583				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>column charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bar charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and bar\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id649433				0	ga	\<variable id=\"type_column_bar\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3430585				0	ga	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826960				0	ga	Colún				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2244026				0	ga	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with vertical bars. The height of each bar is proportional to its value. The x axis shows categories. The y axis shows the value for each category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id1281167				0	ga	Normal - this subtype shows all data values belonging to a category next to each other. Main focus is on the individual absolute values, compared to every other value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3249000				0	ga	Stacked - this subtype shows the data values of each category on top of each other. Main focus is the overall category value and the individual contribution of each value within its category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6968901				0	ga	Percent - this subtype shows the relative percentage of each data value with regard to the total of its category. Main focus is the relative contribution of each value to the category's total.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	ga	You can enable a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D view\</link\> of the data values. The "realistic" scheme tries to give the best 3D look. The "simple" scheme tries to mimic the chart view of other Office products.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id7359233				0	ga	For 3D charts, you can select the shape of each data value from Box, Cylinder, Cone, and Pyramid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id955839				0	ga	Barra				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6596881				0	ga	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with horizontal bars. The length of each bar is proportional to its value. The y axis shows categories. The x axis shows the value for each category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id8750572				0	ga	The subtypes are the same as for the Column type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Trend Lines 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	bm_id1744743				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;regression curves\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>regression curves in charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>trend lines in charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mean value lines in charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id5409405				0	ga	\<variable id=\"regression\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050100.xhp\"\>Trend Lines\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id143436				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>No trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5716727				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A linear trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5840021				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A logarithmic trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9417096				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>An exponential trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8482924				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A power trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8962370				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the trend line equation next to the trend line.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6889858				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the coefficient of determination next to the trend line.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8398998				0	ga	If you insert a trend line to a chart type that uses categories, like \<emph\>Line \</emph\>or \<emph\>Column, \</emph\>then the numbers 1, 2, 3, \<emph\>…\</emph\> are used as x-values to calculate the trend line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5676747				0	ga	To insert trend lines for all data series, double-click the chart to enter edit mode. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Lines\</item\>, then select the type of trend line from None, Linear, Logarithmic, Exponential, or Power trend line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4349192				0	ga	To insert a trend line for a single data series, select the data series in the chart, right-click to open the context menu, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Line\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9337443				0	ga	To delete a single trend line or mean value line, click the line, then press the Del key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4529251				0	ga	To delete all trend lines, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Lines\</item\>, then select \<emph\>None\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id296334				0	ga	A trend line is shown in the legend automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4072084				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Mean Value Lines are special trend lines that show the mean value. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Mean Value Lines\</item\> to insert mean value lines for data series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9569689				0	ga	The trend line has the same color as the corresponding data series. To change the line properties, select the trend line and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Format Selection - Line\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id846888				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To show the trend line equation, select the trend line in the chart, right-click to open the context menu, and choose \<emph\>Insert Trend Line Equation\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8962065				0	ga	When the chart is in edit mode, %PRODUCTNAME gives you the equation of the trend line and the coefficient of determination R². Click on the trend line to see the information in the status bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7735221				0	ga	You can also calculate the parameters using Calc functions as follows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id5744193				0	ga	The linear regression equation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9251991				0	ga	The \<emph\>linear regression\</emph\> follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=m*x+b\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7951902				0	ga	m = SLOPE(Data_Y;Data_X) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6637165				0	ga	b = INTERCEPT(Data_Y ;Data_X) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7879268				0	ga	Calculate the coefficient of determination by				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9244361				0	ga	r² = RSQ(Data_Y;Data_X) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2083498				0	ga	Besides m, b and r² the array function \<emph\>LINEST\</emph\> provides additional statistics for a regression analysis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id2538834				0	ga	The logarithm regression equation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id394299				0	ga	The \<emph\>logarithm regression\</emph\> follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=a*ln(x)+b\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2134159				0	ga	a = SLOPE(Data_Y;LN(Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5946531				0	ga	b = INTERCEPT(Data_Y ;LN(Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5649281				0	ga	r² = RSQ(Data_Y;LN(Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7874080				0	ga	The exponential regression equation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9112216				0	ga	The exponential regression follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*exp(a*x)\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*m^x\</item\>, which is transformed to \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+a*x\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+ln(m)*x\</item\> respectively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4416638				0	ga	a = SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);Data_X) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1039155				0	ga	The variables for the second variation are calculated as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7184057				0	ga	m = EXP(SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id786767				0	ga	b = EXP(INTERCEPT(LN(Data_Y);Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7127292				0	ga	Calculate the coefficient of determination by				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5437177				0	ga	r² = RSQ(LN(Data_Y);Data_X) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6946317				0	ga	Besides m, b and r² the array function LOGEST provides additional statistics for a regression analysis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id6349375				0	ga	The power regression equation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1857661				0	ga	 For \<emph\>power regression\</emph\> curves a transformation to a linear model takes place. The power regression follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*x^a\</item\> , which is transformed to \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+a*ln(x)\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8517105				0	ga	a = SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9827265				0	ga	b = EXP(INTERCEPT(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2357249				0	ga	r² = RSQ(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id9204077				0	ga	Constraints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7393719				0	ga	 The calculation of the trend line considers only data pairs with the following values:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7212744				0	ga	logarithm regression: only positive x-values are considered,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1664479				0	ga	exponential regression: only positive y-values are considered,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8734702				0	ga	power regression: only positive x-values and positive y-values are considered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id181279				0	ga	You should transform your data accordingly; it is best to work on a copy of the original data and transform the copied data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7907040				0	ga	The polynomial regression equation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8918729				0	ga	A \<emph\>polynomial regression\</emph\> curve cannot be added automatically. You must calculate this curve manually. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id33875				0	ga	Create a table with the columns x, x², x³, … , xⁿ, y up to the desired degree n. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8720053				0	ga	Use the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=LINEST(Data_Y,Data_X)\</item\> with the complete range x to xⁿ (without headings) as Data_X. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5068514				0	ga	The first row of the LINEST output contains the coefficients of the regression polynomial, with the coefficient of xⁿ at the leftmost position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8202154				0	ga	The first element of the third row of the LINEST output is the value of r². See the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#Section8\"\>LINEST\</link\> function for details on proper use and an explanation of the other output parameters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4562211				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\"\>Y Error Bars tab page\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Smooth Line Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3803827				0	ga	\<bookmark_value\>curves;properties in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties;smooth lines in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3050325				0	ga	Smooth Line Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id9421979				0	ga	In a chart that displays lines (Line type or XY type), you can choose to show curves instead of straight lines. Some options control the properties of those curves.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id1228370				0	ga	To change line properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1601611				0	ga	Select Cubic Spline or B-Spline.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id879848				0	ga	These are mathematical models that influence the display of the curves. The cubic spline line passes through all points, while the B-spline line connects the first and last point and passes by the intermediate points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3464461				0	ga	Optionally set the resolution. A higher value leads to a smoother line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	ga	For B-spline lines optionally set the data points order.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a cubic spline model.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1068758				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a B-spline model.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id2320932				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the resolution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id8638874				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the data points order.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ga	Tábla Sonraí				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150869				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"Data Table\"\>Data Table\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115	2			0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramData\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Data Table \</emph\>dialog where you can edit the chart data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	51			0	ga	The\<emph\> Data Table \</emph\>dialog is not available if you insert a chart that is based on a Calc sheet or on a Writer table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6746421				0	ga	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06990000.xhp\"\>To update a chart manually when a Writer table got changed\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id2565996				0	ga	Some changes will become visible only after you close and reopen the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id6129947				0	ga	To change chart data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	ga	When you create a chart that is based on default data, or when you copy a chart into your document, you can open the Data Table dialog to enter your own data. The chart responds to the data in a live preview.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9487594				0	ga	Close the Chart Data dialog to apply all changes to the chart. Choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to cancel the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id4149906				0	ga	Insert or select a chart that is not based on existing cell data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6064943				0	ga	Choose \<emph\>View - Chart Data Table\</emph\> to open the Data Table dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	ga	The data series are organized in columns. The role of the left most column is set to categories or data labels respectively. The contents of the left most column are always formatted as text. You can insert more text columns to be used as hierarchical labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9799798				0	ga	Click a cell in the dialog and change the contents. Click another cell to see the changed contents in the preview.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	ga	Enter the name of the data series in the text box above the column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id743430				0	ga	Use the icons above the table to insert or delete rows and columns. For data series with multiple columns, only whole data series can be inserted or deleted. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	ga	The order of the data series in the chart is the same as in the data table. Use the \<emph\>Move Series Right\</emph\> icon to switch the current column with its neighbor on the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	ga	The order of the categories or data points in the chart is the same as in the data table. Use the \<emph\>Move Row Down\</emph\> icon to switch the current row with its neighbor below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new row below the current row.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new data series after the current column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152297				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new text column after the current column for hierarchical axes descriptions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159231				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the current row. It is not possible to delete the label row.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153336				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the current series or text column. It is not possible to delete the first text column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id4089175				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Switches the current column with its neighbor at the right.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3949095				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Switches the current row with its neighbor below.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id6697286				0	ga	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter names for the data series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
